window.CLF_EXAMS=window.CLF_EXAMS||[];
window.CLF_EXAMS.push({"id":2,"qs":[{"id":"E2B-37","d":2,"ts":"2.3.2","t":"S3 Lifecycle and small objects","q":"An IoT ingestion process writes about 80 million JSON objects per month to Amazon S3. The average object size is 8 KB. After 30 days the objects are rarely read. A data engineer proposed a Lifecycle rule that transitions every object to S3 Standard-IA after 30 days, but the expected savings did not appear. Which solution will reduce storage cost MOST effectively?","o":["Shorten the Lifecycle rule so that objects transition to S3 Standard-IA after 1 day.","Use a daily AWS Glue job to compact the small JSON objects into large Parquet files, and apply Lifecycle transitions to the compacted files.","Transition the objects to S3 One Zone-IA instead of S3 Standard-IA after 30 days.","Enable S3 Versioning so that Lifecycle rules apply to all object versions."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: '80 million ... objects' dengan 'average object size is 8 KB'. Objek kecil adalah jebakan klasik: Standard-IA menagih minimal 128 KB per objek, setiap transisi lifecycle dikenai biaya per request, dan sejak September 2024 perilaku default S3 Lifecycle tidak mentransisikan objek di bawah 128 KB ke storage class mana pun (kecuali Anda menambahkan object size filter). Itu sebabnya penghematan tidak muncul: objek 8 KB tetap di Standard, dan kalaupun dipaksa transisi, tagihan minimum 128 KB plus biaya request membuatnya lebih mahal. Mengompaksi banyak file kecil menjadi file Parquet besar mengurangi jumlah objek, biaya request dan ukuran (kolumnar dan terkompresi), lalu transisi lifecycle pada file besar benar-benar efektif dan query juga lebih cepat. Mempercepat transisi atau memilih One Zone-IA tetap terkena aturan minimum ukuran dan biaya request. Versioning tidak relevan. Ingat: banyak objek kecil → compact dulu, baru tiering.","r":["Salah — Mempercepat transisi tidak menyelesaikan akar masalah: objek <128 KB secara default tidak ditransisikan, dan kalaupun dipaksa dengan size filter, Standard-IA menagih minimal 128 KB per objek ditambah biaya transisi per objek (dan minimum durasi penyimpanan 30 hari).","Benar — Kompaksi mengurangi jumlah objek dan ukuran data sehingga transisi lifecycle berikutnya benar-benar hemat.","Salah — One Zone-IA juga punya minimum tagihan 128 KB per objek dan biaya transisi per objek, dan objek <128 KB tetap tidak ditransisikan secara default.","Salah — Versioning malah menambah versi yang disimpan dan tidak mengurangi biaya."],"k":"Tips ujian: lifecycle untuk jutaan objek kecil (<128 KB) tidak hemat → compact/aggregate dulu."},{"id":"E3B-39","d":3,"ts":"3.4.1","t":"AWS Glue Data Quality in ETL jobs","q":"An AWS Glue ETL job loads daily order files into an Amazon S3 curated zone. The business requires that the load is stopped and no data is written to the curated zone if any record has an empty order_id. The team wants to use a managed capability inside the existing job. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Run an AWS Glue crawler on the curated zone after each load and check the schema.","Add an Evaluate Data Quality transform with the rule IsComplete \"order_id\" before the target, and configure the job to fail when data quality fails.","Run an AWS Glue DataBrew profile job on the curated zone every evening.","Query the curated zone with Amazon Athena after the load to count null order_id values."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'stopped and no data is written' bila ada order_id kosong, serta 'managed capability inside the existing job'. AWS Glue Data Quality dapat dijalankan di dalam job ETL melalui transform Evaluate Data Quality dengan aturan DQDL IsComplete \"order_id\". Opsi 'Fail job when data quality fails' menghentikan job SEBELUM data ditulis ke target. Distraktor terdekat adalah DataBrew profile job atau query Athena: keduanya memeriksa SETELAH data dimuat sehingga data buruk sudah masuk curated zone. Crawler hanya melihat skema, bukan nilai kosong. Aturan: cek kualitas data saat pemrosesan dan blokir load → Glue Data Quality di job ETL dengan fail-on-failure.","r":["Salah — Crawler mendeteksi skema, bukan nilai kosong pada kolom, dan berjalan setelah data dimuat.","Benar — Evaluate Data Quality dengan IsComplete dan opsi fail job memblokir penulisan bila ada order_id kosong.","Salah — Profiling setelah load terlambat karena data buruk sudah masuk curated zone.","Salah — Pemeriksaan setelah load tidak mencegah data buruk ditulis."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'stop the job before writing bad data' → Glue Data Quality in ETL + fail job on failure."},{"id":"E4A-27","d":4,"ts":"4.1.7","t":"SageMaker Unified Studio project profiles","q":"A domain administrator in Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio wants analysts in the marketing domain unit to create only SQL analytics projects that use Amazon Athena and Amazon Redshift Serverless. Analysts must not be able to provision Amazon EMR clusters from their projects. Other business units must keep their current capabilities. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Delete the EMR blueprints from the domain.","Attach a permissions boundary to each analyst's IAM user that denies elasticmapreduce actions.","Create a separate SageMaker Unified Studio domain for the marketing analysts.","Create a project profile that includes only the required SQL analytics blueprints, and authorize only the marketing domain unit to use that project profile for project creation."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'create only SQL analytics projects' dan 'other business units must keep their current capabilities'. Project profile adalah template project yang berisi kumpulan blueprint; ia menentukan tool dan resource apa yang bisa dipakai di project. Dengan membuat project profile yang hanya berisi blueprint SQL analytics (Athena/lakehouse dan Redshift Serverless) lalu mengatur otorisasinya hanya untuk marketing domain unit, analis marketing tidak dapat membuat project dengan EMR. Menghapus blueprint EMR dari domain akan berdampak ke semua unit bisnis. Permissions boundary pada IAM user tidak cocok karena resource project diprovisikan oleh role project dan pengguna bisa datang dari IdP, sehingga kontrol di level IAM user tidak tepat sasaran. Domain terpisah memecah catalog dan menambah overhead. Aturan umum: batasi tool per kelompok → project profile + otorisasi per domain unit.","r":["Salah — Menghapus blueprint dari domain memengaruhi semua unit bisnis, bukan hanya marketing.","Salah — Project resource diprovisikan lewat role project, sehingga boundary pada IAM user bukan kontrol yang tepat dan sulit dikelola.","Salah — Domain terpisah menambah overhead dan memecah business catalog.","Benar — Project profile dengan blueprint terbatas yang diotorisasi untuk domain unit marketing membatasi tool tanpa memengaruhi unit lain."],"k":"Tips ujian: kontrol tool/resource yang boleh dibuat project → project profile (kumpulan blueprint) + otorisasi per domain unit."},{"id":"E3B-14","d":3,"ts":"3.3.2","t":"CloudWatch cross-account observability","q":"A company runs AWS Glue and Amazon EMR pipelines in 15 workload accounts. A central operations team wants to search logs and view metrics and alarms from all 15 accounts in a single CloudWatch console without switching roles. The solution must require the LEAST ongoing effort. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Configure CloudWatch cross-account observability with a central monitoring account and link the 15 workload accounts as source accounts.","Create subscription filters in every account that stream logs to a central Amazon Data Firehose stream and query the logs in S3 with Athena.","Give operators IAM roles in each account and switch roles to view each account's CloudWatch console.","Deploy a self-managed Grafana server on Amazon EC2 in each account."],"a":[0],"e":"Persyaratannya: 'single CloudWatch console', 'logs, metrics and alarms', 'without switching roles', dan 'LEAST ongoing effort'. CloudWatch cross-account observability menghubungkan source accounts ke satu monitoring account sehingga metrics, logs, dan traces dari semua akun bisa dicari dan divisualisasikan langsung (bisa diatur lewat AWS Organizations). Distraktor terdekat adalah subscription filter ke Firehose + Athena: hanya menangani log (bukan metrik/alarm), perlu pipeline di 15 akun, dan bukan pengalaman CloudWatch console. Switch role melanggar syarat eksplisit. Grafana self-managed per akun menambah overhead server. Aturan: monitoring terpusat multi-akun native → CloudWatch cross-account observability.","r":["Benar — Cross-account observability memberi satu monitoring account yang dapat melihat logs, metrics, dan alarms semua source account.","Salah — Hanya memusatkan log, butuh pipeline di setiap akun, dan tidak memusatkan metrik maupun alarm.","Salah — Persyaratan secara eksplisit melarang berpindah role antar akun.","Salah — Grafana self-managed per akun menambah server yang harus dirawat dan tetap tidak terpusat."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'single pane of glass across accounts' di CloudWatch → cross-account observability (monitoring account)."},{"id":"E2B-26","d":2,"ts":"2.2.6","t":"SageMaker Catalog subscriptions","q":"A company uses Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio. Producer teams publish Lake Formation-managed AWS Glue tables to Amazon SageMaker Catalog. Consumers in other projects must be able to find a dataset, request access with a business justification, and receive access only after the data owner approves. The company wants access to be granted automatically after approval, without tickets to the platform team. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Have consumers email the platform team, which then grants Lake Formation permissions manually.","Have consumers submit a subscription request for the published asset in SageMaker Catalog; after the producer project approves it, the catalog grants access to the consumer project automatically.","Share the S3 buckets with the consumer accounts by using bucket policies and AWS RAM.","Create an IAM role for every consumer with read access to the S3 prefixes and distribute the role ARNs."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'request access with a business justification', 'only after the data owner approves' dan 'granted automatically after approval'. SageMaker Catalog (dibangun di atas Amazon DataZone) menyediakan alur subscription: konsumen mencari asset yang dipublikasikan, mengirim subscription request beserta alasan, owner/producer meninjau lalu menyetujui atau menolak. Setelah disetujui, catalog memenuhi langganan secara otomatis, misalnya dengan grant Lake Formation untuk tabel Glue yang dikelola Lake Formation, ke project konsumen. Email dan grant manual memenuhi persetujuan, tetapi justru bergantung pada tiket ke tim platform. Bucket policy, RAM, atau role IAM per konsumen tidak punya alur request/approval dan memberi akses di level S3 yang kasar. Ingat: 'request → approve → auto-grant' untuk data → subscription di SageMaker Catalog.","r":["Salah — Proses manual lewat email adalah alur tiket yang ingin dihilangkan dan sulit diaudit.","Benar — Subscription request dengan approval producer dan fulfillment otomatis adalah fitur inti SageMaker Catalog.","Salah — Bucket policy/RAM tidak menyediakan alur permintaan dan persetujuan, dan memberi akses S3 yang kasar.","Salah — Role IAM per konsumen menambah overhead dan melewati persetujuan owner data."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'subscribe', 'request access', 'approval workflow' → Amazon SageMaker Catalog subscription requests."},{"id":"E4A-15","d":4,"ts":"4.1.4","t":"Cross-account role assumption with AWS CLI","q":"Data engineers sign in to a development AWS account with IAM users. They occasionally need to run AWS CLI commands in a production account to troubleshoot pipelines. The security team requires short-lived credentials, MFA for production access, and no IAM users in the production account. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create a role in the production account whose trust policy allows the development account and requires aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent, and configure an AWS CLI profile with role_arn, source_profile, and mfa_serial.","Create IAM users for the engineers in the production account and enforce MFA through an IAM policy.","Share the access keys of a production IAM user in AWS Secrets Manager and grant the engineers access to the secret.","Run aws sts get-session-token with MFA in the development account and use the returned credentials directly against the production account."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'short-lived credentials', 'MFA', 'no IAM users in the production account'. Pola standar akses lintas akun adalah role assumption: role di akun produksi memiliki trust policy yang mempercayai akun development, dengan kondisi aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent bernilai true. Profil AWS CLI dengan role_arn, source_profile, dan mfa_serial membuat CLI otomatis memanggil sts:AssumeRole dengan kode MFA dan memakai credential sementara. Membuat IAM user di produksi melanggar syarat. Berbagi access key produksi berarti credential jangka panjang dan tidak dapat diaudit per orang. get-session-token menghasilkan credential sementara untuk akun development saja, tidak berlaku di akun lain. Aturan umum: akses lintas akun = role di akun tujuan + trust policy + sts:AssumeRole.","r":["Benar — Role lintas akun dengan syarat MFA dan profil CLI berbasis role memberi credential sementara tanpa IAM user di produksi.","Salah — Melanggar syarat tidak ada IAM user di akun produksi.","Salah — Access key bersama adalah credential jangka panjang dan tidak bisa ditelusuri per engineer.","Salah — Credential dari get-session-token hanya berlaku untuk identitas di akun development, bukan untuk resource akun produksi."],"k":"Tips ujian: akses lintas akun + MFA → sts:AssumeRole ke role di akun tujuan dengan kondisi aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent."},{"id":"E3A-60","d":3,"ts":"3.2.5","t":"Redshift Serverless for intermittent workloads","q":"A data science team runs SQL analysis on a 2 TB dataset in Amazon Redshift only a few times per week, with unpredictable timing and long idle periods between sessions. Occasionally, a monthly report needs much more compute for an hour. The team does not want to resize clusters, schedule pauses, or plan capacity. Which solution is MOST cost-effective?","o":["Amazon Redshift Serverless, which scales compute automatically and charges only for the RPU capacity used while queries run.","An Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster sized for the monthly peak and running continuously.","An Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster with a scheduled pause and resume every night.","An Amazon EMR on EC2 cluster with Presto that runs continuously."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'few times per week', 'unpredictable timing', 'long idle periods', 'occasional peak', dan 'no resize, pause scheduling, or capacity planning'. Redshift Serverless menskalakan kapasitas (RPU) secara otomatis sesuai beban dan hanya menagih RPU-hour saat query berjalan (ditagih per detik), sehingga waktu idle tidak dikenai biaya compute. Beban puncak bulanan ditangani dengan scaling otomatis tanpa resize manual. Cluster provisioned berukuran puncak yang terus menyala membayar kapasitas besar yang sebagian besar idle. Jadwal pause/resume tidak cocok karena waktu penggunaan tidak terduga dan tetap memerlukan pengelolaan. EMR dengan Presto yang terus menyala mahal dan menambah overhead. Aturan umum: beban intermittent dan tidak terduga → serverless (bayar sesuai penggunaan).","r":["Benar — Serverless menskalakan otomatis dan hanya menagih saat query berjalan, ideal untuk penggunaan sporadis.","Salah — Membayar kapasitas puncak 24/7 padahal sebagian besar waktu idle.","Salah — Waktu penggunaan tidak terduga, sehingga jadwal pause/resume rumit dan bisa mengganggu pengguna.","Salah — Cluster yang selalu menyala mahal dan harus dikelola."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'unpredictable, intermittent, no capacity planning' → Redshift Serverless."},{"id":"E2C-03","d":2,"ts":"2.4.1","t":"Redshift SUPER data type for semi-structured data","q":"A company ingests JSON events from dozens of partner applications into Amazon Redshift. Each partner adds new nested attributes several times a month, and analysts need to query both existing and newly added attributes with SQL soon after the data arrives. The company wants to avoid changing the table definition every time a partner adds an attribute. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Flatten every JSON document with an AWS Glue job into a wide relational table and add new columns with ALTER TABLE whenever a new attribute appears.","Store the raw JSON as VARCHAR(65535) and parse attributes at query time with string functions such as JSON_EXTRACT_PATH_TEXT.","Load the JSON documents into a column of the SUPER data type and query nested attributes with PartiQL dot and bracket notation.","Convert the JSON to CSV with AWS Lambda before loading so that the COPY command can map columns by position."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah semi-structured data yang atributnya sering berubah dan 'avoid changing the table definition'. Tipe data SUPER di Amazon Redshift menyimpan data semi-structured (JSON nested) secara schemaless, dan PartiQL memungkinkan query atribut nested dengan dot/bracket notation tanpa harus mendefinisikan kolom baru. Atribut baru langsung bisa di-query begitu data dimuat, sehingga overhead perubahan schema hilang. Flatten ke wide table dengan ALTER TABLE setiap ada atribut baru adalah overhead operasional yang justru ingin dihindari. VARCHAR dengan fungsi JSON string bekerja, tetapi lebih lambat, dibatasi ukuran 64 KB, dan parsing ulang setiap query. Konversi ke CSV menghilangkan struktur nested dan rapuh terhadap perubahan urutan kolom. Aturan umum: data semi-structured dengan schema yang berubah-ubah di Redshift → SUPER + PartiQL.","r":["Salah — Pipeline flatten plus ALTER TABLE manual untuk setiap atribut baru menimbulkan overhead operasional tinggi.","Salah — Parsing string JSON pada saat query lebih lambat, terbatas ukuran VARCHAR, dan kurang efisien dibanding SUPER.","Benar — SUPER menyimpan JSON nested secara schemaless dan PartiQL dapat langsung meng-query atribut baru tanpa perubahan DDL.","Salah — CSV kehilangan struktur nested dan mapping berdasarkan posisi rusak saat atribut ditambahkan."],"k":"Tips ujian: JSON semi-structured + schema sering berubah di Redshift → tipe SUPER + PartiQL."},{"id":"E3B-61","d":3,"ts":"3.4.4","t":"Sampling in Athena with TABLESAMPLE","q":"An analyst wants to estimate the average order value from a 5 TB Amazon Athena table quickly and cheaply before running the full query. The estimate should be based on a row-level random sample that is as statistically unbiased as possible. Which query technique should the analyst use?","o":["SELECT avg(amount) FROM orders TABLESAMPLE BERNOULLI (1)","SELECT avg(amount) FROM orders TABLESAMPLE SYSTEM (1)","SELECT avg(amount) FROM orders LIMIT 1000000","SELECT avg(amount) FROM orders WHERE order_id < 1000000"],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'row-level random sample' yang 'as statistically unbiased as possible'. Di Athena, TABLESAMPLE BERNOULLI (p) mengevaluasi setiap baris secara independen dengan probabilitas p persen, sehingga menghasilkan sampel acak per baris. Distraktor terdekat adalah TABLESAMPLE SYSTEM: lebih cepat karena memilih blok/split data secara utuh, tetapi baris dalam satu blok cenderung berkorelasi (misalnya dari file atau periode yang sama), sehingga hasilnya bisa bias. LIMIT tanpa urutan mengembalikan baris pertama yang ditemukan, bukan sampel acak, dan filter order_id bias ke order awal. Aturan: BERNOULLI = per baris, lebih tidak bias; SYSTEM = per blok, lebih cepat tetapi bisa bias.","r":["Benar — BERNOULLI memilih setiap baris secara independen sehingga sampelnya paling tidak bias.","Salah — SYSTEM mengambil blok data utuh sehingga baris yang saling berkorelasi bisa membuat hasil bias.","Salah — LIMIT mengambil baris yang kebetulan dibaca lebih dulu, bukan sampel acak.","Salah — Filter rentang ID bias ke order lama dan bukan sampel acak."],"k":"Tips ujian: Athena TABLESAMPLE BERNOULLI = row-level random; SYSTEM = block-level (faster, more bias)."},{"id":"E2C-25","d":2,"ts":"2.4.3","t":"Homogeneous vs heterogeneous migration","q":"A company is migrating a 2 TB Amazon RDS for MySQL 8.0 database to Amazon Aurora MySQL. A junior engineer proposes creating an AWS DMS Schema Conversion migration project first. The data engineer wants the simplest approach that preserves the schema exactly. What should the data engineer recommend?","o":["Run DMS Schema Conversion to convert the MySQL schema to MySQL, then migrate the data with DMS.","Skip schema conversion because the source and target engines are compatible, and use a homogeneous approach such as an Aurora read replica or snapshot migration.","Convert the schema to PostgreSQL first and then back to MySQL to normalize data types.","Use AWS Glue to rebuild every table definition from a crawler run."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah migrasi homogen (MySQL ke Aurora MySQL) dan 'simplest approach that preserves the schema exactly'. Konversi schema hanya diperlukan pada migrasi heterogen, ketika engine sumber dan target berbeda dialek. Untuk RDS for MySQL ke Aurora MySQL, AWS menyediakan cara native seperti membuat Aurora read replica dari instance RDS for MySQL lalu mempromosikannya, atau migrasi dari snapshot; schema, index, dan objek ikut terbawa apa adanya. DMS Schema Conversion tidak menyediakan jalur MySQL ke MySQL karena tidak dibutuhkan. Konversi bolak-balik ke PostgreSQL justru merusak fidelity schema. Crawler Glue hanya membuat metadata katalog dan tidak membangun ulang tabel database. Aturan umum: homogen → tool native/homogeneous migration; heterogen → DMS Schema Conversion.","r":["Salah — Konversi schema tidak diperlukan dan tidak tersedia untuk jalur MySQL ke MySQL; ini menambah langkah tanpa manfaat.","Benar — Engine kompatibel sehingga read replica atau snapshot migration mempertahankan schema persis dengan usaha paling kecil.","Salah — Konversi bolak-balik antar engine berisiko mengubah tipe data dan objek.","Salah — Crawler Glue hanya membuat metadata katalog, bukan tabel di database target."],"k":"Tips ujian: migrasi homogen → tidak perlu schema conversion; schema conversion hanya untuk heterogen."},{"id":"E1A-48","d":1,"ts":"1.1.8","t":"Firehose IP allowlist for Redshift","q":"An Amazon Data Firehose stream must deliver data to a publicly accessible Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster in a VPC. Delivery fails with connection timeouts. The cluster's security group currently allows inbound traffic only from the corporate network. What should the data engineer do to allow delivery while keeping access restricted?","o":["Attach an IAM policy for Firehose to the cluster's security group.","Allow inbound traffic on the Redshift port from 0.0.0.0/0.","Add inbound rules to the cluster's security group that allow the Redshift port from the Data Firehose CIDR block for the AWS Region.","Create a NAT gateway in the cluster's subnet."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: Firehose ke Redshift 'publicly accessible', 'connection timeouts', dan 'keeping access restricted'. Firehose terhubung ke cluster Redshift dari rentang IP milik layanan Firehose di Region tersebut, sehingga security group cluster harus mengizinkan port Redshift (default 5439) dari CIDR Firehose untuk Region itu, sesuai dokumentasi Firehose. Ini adalah IP allowlist yang terbatas. Distraktor terdekat adalah membuka 0.0.0.0/0: delivery berhasil, tetapi cluster terbuka ke seluruh internet. Security group tidak menerima IAM policy; IAM mengatur izin API, bukan konektivitas jaringan. NAT gateway hanya untuk trafik keluar dari subnet privat, bukan trafik masuk ke cluster. Aturan umum: layanan AWS yang terhubung dari IP publiknya (Firehose ke Redshift/Splunk/HTTP) = allowlist CIDR layanan untuk Region tersebut.","r":["Salah — Security group tidak memakai IAM policy; IAM tidak mengatur konektivitas jaringan.","Salah — 0.0.0.0/0 membuka cluster ke seluruh internet dan melanggar persyaratan.","Benar — Mengizinkan CIDR Firehose untuk Region pada port Redshift membuka akses hanya untuk Firehose.","Salah — NAT gateway hanya untuk trafik keluar dari subnet privat, tidak membuka akses masuk."],"k":"Firehose → Redshift publik timeout → allowlist CIDR Firehose per Region di security group."},{"id":"E1C-37","d":1,"ts":"1.3.4","t":"SNS message filtering","q":"Pipeline components publish alerts to one Amazon SNS topic. Each message has a message attribute named severity with values INFO, WARNING, or CRITICAL. The on-call team's Amazon SQS queue must receive only CRITICAL alerts, while an archive queue must receive all alerts. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Subscribe both queues to the topic and add a subscription filter policy on the on-call queue's subscription that matches severity = CRITICAL.","Subscribe a Lambda function that inspects each message and forwards CRITICAL alerts to the on-call queue.","Create three separate SNS topics and change every publisher to choose the topic based on severity.","Have the on-call consumer read every message and discard non-critical alerts."],"a":[0],"e":"Kebutuhannya: antrean on-call 'only CRITICAL', antrean arsip 'all alerts', dengan 'LEAST operational overhead'. SNS subscription filter policy memungkinkan setiap langganan memfilter berdasarkan message attribute (atau isi pesan), sehingga SNS hanya mengirim pesan yang cocok ke antrean on-call, sedangkan langganan arsip tanpa filter menerima semua. Distractor terdekat adalah Lambda router: hasilnya sama, tetapi menambah kode, biaya invocation, dan titik kegagalan. Memecah ke tiga topik memaksa perubahan di semua publisher. Membuang pesan di sisi konsumen membuang biaya dan memperbesar beban antrean. Aturan umum: routing pesan berdasarkan atribut di SNS → subscription filter policy.","r":["Benar — Filter policy pada langganan on-call mengirim hanya CRITICAL, dan langganan arsip menerima semua tanpa kode tambahan.","Salah — Lambda router adalah kode tambahan untuk fitur yang tersedia secara native.","Salah — Mengubah semua publisher dan mengelola banyak topik menambah overhead.","Salah — Konsumen menerima dan memproses pesan yang tidak relevan."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'subscriber only receives some messages' → SNS subscription filter policy."},{"id":"E1B-13","d":1,"ts":"1.2.1","t":"Right-sizing ECS tasks","q":"A data engineer runs a containerized Python transformation as an Amazon ECS task on AWS Fargate with 2 GB of memory. After the input files grew from 500 MB to 3 GB, the task frequently stops with exit code 137 and the logs show the container was killed while loading data. Which action will resolve the issue with the LEAST effort?","o":["Increase the task-level memory and CPU in the ECS task definition to values that fit the larger input files.","Increase the desired count of the ECS service so that more tasks run in parallel.","Increase the ephemeral storage of the Fargate task to 200 GiB.","Switch the task to the EC2 launch type on t3.micro instances."],"a":[0],"e":"Petunjuk kuncinya adalah 'exit code 137' dan container 'killed while loading data' setelah ukuran input naik, yang menandakan container kehabisan memori (OOM kill). Solusi paling sederhana adalah menaikkan memori (dan CPU yang sepadan) pada task definition, karena Fargate memungkinkan ukuran task yang jauh lebih besar dari 2 GB. Menambah desired count adalah distraktor yang umum, tetapi setiap task tetap memuat file 3 GB dengan memori 2 GB sehingga tetap OOM. Ephemeral storage adalah disk, bukan RAM, jadi tidak mengatasi kekurangan memori. Pindah ke t3.micro justru mengurangi memori dan menambah pengelolaan instance. Aturan umum: exit code 137/OOMKilled pada container → right-size memori task atau proses data secara streaming/chunk.","r":["Benar — Menaikkan memori dan CPU task langsung mengatasi OOM kill dengan perubahan konfigurasi minimal.","Salah — Lebih banyak task tidak menambah memori per task; setiap task tetap kehabisan memori.","Salah — Ephemeral storage menambah disk, bukan memori, sehingga OOM tetap terjadi.","Salah — t3.micro memiliki memori sangat kecil dan menambah beban pengelolaan EC2."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'exit code 137 / OOMKilled' → naikkan memori task/container, bukan menambah jumlah task atau disk."},{"id":"E4B-50","d":4,"ts":"4.5.4","t":"AWS Config aggregator and advanced queries","q":"A company has 30 AWS accounts across 4 Regions. The governance team wants a single place to view configuration changes for all accounts and Regions, and to run SQL-like queries such as listing every S3 bucket that does not have default encryption with AWS KMS. The company has never used AWS CloudTrail Lake. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create a CloudTrail Lake event data store for configuration items and query it with SQL.","Enable AWS Config in all accounts and Regions, create an organization-wide AWS Config aggregator in a delegated administrator account, and use AWS Config advanced queries against the aggregator.","Use AWS Trusted Advisor checks in each account and export the results to a spreadsheet.","Use AWS Systems Manager Inventory to collect resource configurations from all accounts."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'single place' untuk 'all accounts and Regions', melihat 'configuration changes', dan menjalankan 'SQL-like queries' dengan overhead terendah. AWS Config aggregator mengumpulkan data konfigurasi dan compliance dari banyak akun dan Region (bisa untuk seluruh organisasi) ke satu akun, dan advanced query memakai sintaks mirip SQL (SELECT ... WHERE) atas properti konfigurasi resource saat ini di aggregator. Distraktor terdekat adalah CloudTrail Lake: secara fungsi dapat menyimpan configuration item, tetapi CloudTrail Lake tidak menerima pelanggan baru sejak 31 Mei 2026 dan perusahaan ini belum pernah memakainya. Trusted Advisor per akun bersifat manual dan bukan histori konfigurasi. Systems Manager Inventory berfokus pada metadata instance terkelola (software, file), bukan konfigurasi S3. Aturan umum: konfigurasi multi-akun/multi-Region + query → Config aggregator + advanced query. Catatan pembaruan: CloudTrail Lake ditutup untuk pelanggan baru sejak 31 Mei 2026.","r":["Salah — CloudTrail Lake tidak menerima pelanggan baru sejak 31 Mei 2026.","Benar — Config aggregator memusatkan data konfigurasi lintas akun/Region dan advanced query mendukung query mirip SQL.","Salah — Proses per akun manual dan tidak memberi histori konfigurasi yang dapat di-query.","Salah — SSM Inventory mengumpulkan metadata instance terkelola, bukan konfigurasi bucket S3."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'view/query configuration across accounts and Regions' → AWS Config aggregator + advanced queries."},{"id":"E1A-02","d":1,"ts":"1.1.1","t":"Data Firehose format conversion","q":"A company collects application logs in JSON format from thousands of servers. The data must be delivered to Amazon S3 in Apache Parquet format for querying with Amazon Athena. A delay of up to 5 minutes is acceptable. The team wants the solution with the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Send the logs to Amazon Data Firehose, enable record format conversion to Parquet using an AWS Glue Data Catalog table schema, and deliver to Amazon S3.","Send the logs to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams and run an Amazon EMR cluster with Spark Streaming to convert the data to Parquet.","Send the logs to Amazon S3 as JSON and schedule an AWS Glue ETL job every 5 minutes to convert new files to Parquet.","Send the logs to Amazon MSK and use a self-managed Kafka Connect cluster on Amazon EC2 to write Parquet files to Amazon S3."],"a":[0],"e":"Persyaratan kuncinya adalah 'Parquet', 'delay of up to 5 minutes is acceptable', dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Amazon Data Firehose adalah layanan fully managed yang bisa langsung mengonversi JSON ke Parquet/ORC menggunakan skema dari tabel AWS Glue Data Catalog, lalu mengirim ke S3 dengan buffering (latensi near-real-time, sesuai toleransi 5 menit). Tidak ada cluster atau job yang perlu dikelola. Distraktor terdekat adalah Glue ETL job terjadwal: hasilnya sama tetapi menambah job scheduling, tracking file baru, dan biaya start-up job tiap 5 menit. EMR dan Kafka Connect self-managed jelas menambah beban operasional. Aturan umum: streaming ke S3 + konversi format sederhana + near-real-time = Data Firehose.","r":["Benar — Firehose fully managed, mendukung konversi JSON ke Parquet dengan skema Glue Data Catalog, dan latensinya sesuai toleransi 5 menit.","Salah — Bisa berfungsi, tetapi mengelola cluster EMR dan aplikasi Spark Streaming menambah overhead operasional yang besar.","Salah — Glue job tiap 5 menit menambah penjadwalan, pelacakan file, dan biaya start-up; lebih rumit dari Firehose.","Salah — Kafka Connect self-managed di EC2 berarti harus mengelola server, scaling, dan patching."],"k":"Near-real-time ke S3 + convert ke Parquet/ORC + least ops → Data Firehose record format conversion."},{"id":"E1B-02","d":1,"ts":"1.2.5","t":"Amazon EMR vs AWS Glue","q":"A media company processes several petabytes of log data each week with Apache Spark, Apache Hudi, and Presto. The jobs require custom Spark configurations, specific open-source application versions, and custom JAR files installed on every node. The company wants to minimize compute costs for the large, fault-tolerant parts of the workload. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use AWS Glue ETL jobs with the G.8X worker type and enable job bookmarks.","Use AWS Lambda functions orchestrated by AWS Step Functions to process the logs in parallel chunks.","Load the logs into Amazon Redshift and transform them with SQL stored procedures on a provisioned cluster.","Use Amazon EMR with On-Demand Instances for the primary and core nodes and Spot Instances for task nodes, and install custom JARs with bootstrap actions."],"a":[3],"e":"Keputusan ditentukan oleh frasa 'custom Spark configurations, specific open-source application versions, and custom JAR files installed on every node' serta kebutuhan beberapa framework (Spark, Hudi, Presto). Amazon EMR memberi kontrol penuh atas aplikasi open-source, versi release, konfigurasi, dan bootstrap action untuk memasang JAR di setiap node. Untuk biaya, pola terbaik adalah On-Demand untuk primary dan core node (menyimpan HDFS dan koordinasi) serta Spot untuk task node yang hanya menjalankan komputasi dan aman jika diinterupsi. AWS Glue adalah distraktor terdekat, tetapi Glue tidak menjalankan Presto dan kontrol atas versi aplikasi serta instalasi di tiap node lebih terbatas. Lambda tidak cocok untuk skala petabyte dengan framework Spark, dan Redshift bukan mesin untuk Hudi/Presto. Aturan umum: butuh kontrol penuh atas ekosistem Hadoop/Spark dan skala sangat besar → Amazon EMR, dengan Spot di task node untuk menekan biaya.","r":["Salah — Glue adalah Spark serverless dengan kontrol terbatas atas versi dan instalasi per node, dan tidak menjalankan Presto.","Salah — Lambda tidak dirancang untuk pemrosesan petabyte dengan Spark/Hudi/Presto dan dibatasi 15 menit per invocation.","Salah — Redshift memproses data dengan SQL, bukan menjalankan Spark, Hudi, dan Presto dengan JAR kustom.","Benar — EMR memberi kontrol penuh atas aplikasi dan konfigurasi, bootstrap action memasang JAR, dan Spot di task node memangkas biaya untuk bagian yang toleran gangguan."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'custom versions/JARs, Presto/Hudi/HBase, full control' → Amazon EMR; 'reduce cost' → Spot untuk task node, bukan primary node."},{"id":"E3A-45","d":3,"ts":"3.2.4","t":"Athena Spark session cost control","q":"A data science team uses Amazon Athena notebooks with the Apache Spark engine. The monthly bill shows high DPU-hour charges even though most notebooks run only a few short calculations. Investigation shows that the sessions use a session idle timeout of 480 minutes, so they often stay open for hours after the last cell runs. Which TWO actions will reduce cost without limiting how the team explores data? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Lower the session idle timeout for the notebook sessions (for example, back to the default of 20 minutes).","Switch the workgroup to Athena SQL engine version 3.","Ask users to end (terminate) their sessions when they finish exploring.","Enable query result reuse for the notebooks.","Increase the coordinator DPU size so calculations finish faster."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'sessions stay open for hours after the last cell runs' dan biaya 'DPU-hour'. Session Athena for Apache Spark ditagih per DPU-hour selama session aktif, termasuk waktu idle sampai idle timeout tercapai. Session idle timeout bisa diatur antara 1 dan 480 menit (default 20 menit). Menurunkan idle timeout membuat session yang ditinggalkan berakhir lebih cepat, dan mengakhiri session secara eksplisit setelah selesai langsung menghentikan tagihan. Keduanya tidak membatasi cara tim bereksplorasi. Athena SQL engine version 3 adalah engine SQL; memindahkan workgroup ke engine SQL justru menghilangkan Spark. Query result reuse adalah fitur query SQL, bukan untuk kalkulasi notebook. DPU yang lebih besar justru menaikkan tarif per jam dan tidak mengatasi waktu idle. Aturan umum: biaya Spark serverless interaktif didorong oleh durasi session, jadi kendalikan idle timeout dan akhiri session.","r":["Benar — Idle timeout yang lebih pendek mengakhiri session yang ditinggalkan sehingga DPU-hour idle berkurang.","Salah — Athena SQL engine version 3 adalah engine SQL; tidak mengurangi biaya session Spark dan malah menghilangkan kemampuan PySpark.","Benar — Mengakhiri session setelah selesai langsung menghentikan tagihan DPU.","Salah — Result reuse hanya berlaku untuk query SQL, bukan kalkulasi Spark.","Salah — DPU lebih besar menaikkan biaya per jam dan tidak mengurangi waktu idle."],"k":"Tips ujian: biaya Athena Spark tinggi karena session idle → turunkan session idle timeout + akhiri session."},{"id":"E2A-02","d":2,"ts":"2.1.1","t":"Amazon MSK tiered storage","q":"A company runs dozens of Apache Kafka producer and consumer applications on a self-managed Kafka cluster in its data center. The company wants to move to AWS without changing application code and must retain topic data for 90 days for reprocessing. Most consumers read only the latest few hours of data. The solution must be MOST cost-effective and minimize operational overhead.","o":["Migrate to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams with a 90-day retention period and rewrite the clients to use the Kinesis Producer Library.","Install Apache Kafka on Amazon EC2 instances with large Amazon EBS volumes sized for 90 days of data.","Migrate to an Amazon MSK provisioned cluster that uses Standard brokers with tiered storage enabled, and set topic retention to 90 days.","Migrate to an Amazon MSK provisioned cluster and size the broker EBS volumes to hold 90 days of data on primary storage."],"a":[2],"e":"Persyaratan kunci: 'without changing application code', retention '90 days', konsumsi mayoritas hanya data terbaru, serta 'MOST cost-effective' dan overhead minimal. Amazon MSK kompatibel dengan API Apache Kafka sehingga aplikasi tidak perlu ditulis ulang. Fitur tiered storage di MSK (untuk Standard brokers) memindahkan segmen data lama ke storage tier berbiaya rendah sementara data panas tetap di EBS broker, cocok untuk retensi panjang yang jarang dibaca. Distraktor terdekat adalah MSK dengan EBS besar: berfungsi, tetapi membayar storage primer yang mahal untuk data yang jarang dibaca. Kinesis Data Streams melanggar syarat 'without changing application code', dan Kafka di EC2 menambah overhead operasional. Aturan umum: workload Kafka yang ingin managed → MSK; retensi panjang murah → tiered storage.","r":["Salah — Kinesis Data Streams tidak kompatibel dengan protokol Kafka, sehingga semua aplikasi harus diubah.","Salah — Kafka self-managed di EC2 membuat tim tetap mengelola patching, scaling, dan recovery broker; overhead tinggi.","Benar — MSK menjaga kompatibilitas Kafka dan tiered storage menyimpan data lama dengan biaya rendah untuk retensi 90 hari.","Salah — Bisa berjalan, tetapi menyimpan 90 hari data di EBS broker jauh lebih mahal dibanding tiered storage untuk data yang jarang dibaca."],"k":"Kafka tanpa ubah kode → Amazon MSK; retensi panjang dan murah → MSK tiered storage."},{"id":"E1B-37","d":1,"ts":"1.2.4","t":"Intermediate staging cost management","q":"A multi-step data pipeline writes intermediate staging files to an S3 prefix named staging/ between AWS Glue jobs. The final curated output is written to a separate prefix. The staging files are needed only for reruns within 7 days, but they have accumulated to hundreds of terabytes over two years. Which solution will reduce storage costs with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create an AWS Lambda function that runs daily, lists the staging/ prefix, and deletes objects older than 7 days.","Create an S3 Lifecycle rule scoped to the staging/ prefix that expires objects 7 days after creation.","Move the staging/ prefix to the S3 Glacier Deep Archive storage class with a Lifecycle rule after 1 day.","Enable S3 Versioning on the bucket so that old staging files can be recovered if needed."],"a":[1],"e":"Penentunya adalah data staging perantara yang hanya dibutuhkan 'within 7 days' namun menumpuk hingga ratusan terabyte, dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. S3 Lifecycle rule dengan filter prefix staging/ dan aksi expiration setelah 7 hari menghapus objek secara otomatis tanpa kode. Lambda yang menghapus objek bisa bekerja, tetapi menambah kode, biaya LIST, dan pemeliharaan. Glacier Deep Archive tetap menyimpan data yang tidak dibutuhkan dan membuat rerun dalam 7 hari menjadi lambat karena restore memakan waktu berjam-jam. Versioning justru menambah biaya karena versi lama ikut disimpan. Aturan umum: data perantara/temporary di S3 → Lifecycle expiration berbasis prefix atau tag.","r":["Salah — Berfungsi, tetapi menambah kode dan pemeliharaan dibanding fitur bawaan.","Benar — Lifecycle expiration pada prefix staging/ menghapus data lama otomatis tanpa kode.","Salah — Data yang tidak dibutuhkan tetap tersimpan, dan restore Deep Archive menghambat rerun.","Salah — Versioning menambah jumlah data yang disimpan dan biaya."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'temporary/staging data no longer needed after N days' → S3 Lifecycle expiration rule (prefix filter)."},{"id":"E4B-02","d":4,"ts":"4.3.1","t":"Glue sensitive data detection and redaction","q":"A company ingests CSV files from partners into an Amazon S3 raw zone. Some free-text columns occasionally contain email addresses and phone numbers, but the affected columns are not known in advance. Before the data is written to the curated zone, any detected PII must be redacted. The data engineering team wants to write as little custom code as possible. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Run Amazon Macie sensitive data discovery jobs on the raw zone and use an AWS Lambda function to rewrite each object that has a finding.","Use AWS Lake Formation column-level permissions to hide the free-text columns from all consumers of the curated zone.","Add the Detect Sensitive Data transform in an AWS Glue Studio visual ETL job, configure it to scan all columns for email and phone number patterns, and set the action to redact detected values before writing to the curated zone.","Encrypt the curated zone with SSE-KMS using a customer managed key so that PII cannot be read by unauthorized users."],"a":[2],"e":"Syarat penentu: PII harus 'redacted' sebelum ditulis ke curated zone, kolomnya 'not known in advance', dan 'as little custom code as possible'. AWS Glue menyediakan transform Detect Sensitive Data (sensitive data detection) yang dapat memindai seluruh kolom dengan managed pattern seperti email dan nomor telepon, lalu langsung melakukan aksi redact/hash pada nilai yang terdeteksi di dalam pipeline ETL. Ini menyelesaikan deteksi dan masking di satu langkah tanpa kode kustom. Distraktor terdekat adalah Macie + Lambda: Macie memang mendeteksi PII di S3, tetapi tidak meredaksi, sehingga Anda tetap harus menulis Lambda untuk parsing dan rewrite objek, dan prosesnya terpisah dari pipeline. Lake Formation column permission menyembunyikan seluruh kolom (kehilangan data non-PII) dan PII tetap tersimpan. Enkripsi at rest tidak meredaksi apa pun; user yang berwenang tetap melihat PII. Aturan umum: deteksi + redaksi PII di dalam pipeline Glue → Glue Detect Sensitive Data transform.","r":["Salah — Macie hanya menghasilkan findings; redaksi tetap membutuhkan kode kustom Lambda di luar pipeline.","Salah — Menyembunyikan kolom utuh tidak meredaksi PII, data non-PII di kolom itu ikut hilang, dan PII tetap tersimpan.","Benar — Glue Detect Sensitive Data memindai semua kolom dan meredaksi PII secara inline tanpa kode kustom.","Salah — Enkripsi at rest melindungi media penyimpanan, bukan menghapus PII dari data yang dibaca pengguna berizin."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'detect and redact PII inside an ETL job, low code' → AWS Glue Detect Sensitive Data transform; Macie = discovery di S3 saja."},{"id":"E2B-02","d":2,"ts":"2.2.1","t":"Redshift Spectrum with Glue Data Catalog","q":"A data engineering team runs an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster that holds 2 years of curated sales data. Five years of older clickstream data is stored as Parquet in Amazon S3 and is already cataloged in the AWS Glue Data Catalog database 'clickstream_db'. Analysts must join the clickstream data with the Redshift sales tables in a single SQL query without loading the clickstream data into Redshift. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Create an Amazon Redshift federated query to the AWS Glue Data Catalog and join the remote tables.","Run a nightly COPY command that loads the clickstream Parquet files into Redshift staging tables.","Create an external schema in Redshift that references 'clickstream_db' in the AWS Glue Data Catalog, and query the tables through Amazon Redshift Spectrum.","Use Amazon Athena to UNLOAD the Redshift sales tables into Amazon S3 and join the data in Athena."],"a":[2],"e":"Syarat yang menentukan adalah 'join ... in a single SQL query' dan 'without loading the clickstream data into Redshift'. CREATE EXTERNAL SCHEMA ... FROM DATA CATALOG membuat Redshift membaca definisi tabel dari Glue Data Catalog, lalu Redshift Spectrum memindai Parquet langsung di S3 dan hasilnya bisa di-join dengan tabel lokal. Ini persis cara memakai technical catalog untuk mengonsumsi data dari lokasi aslinya. Federated query di Redshift ditujukan untuk database operasional seperti Aurora/RDS PostgreSQL dan MySQL, bukan untuk Glue Data Catalog. COPY malam hari melanggar syarat 'without loading'. Ingat: Redshift + data S3 yang sudah di-catalog → external schema + Redshift Spectrum.","r":["Salah — Federated query Redshift menghubungkan ke Aurora/RDS PostgreSQL dan MySQL, bukan ke Glue Data Catalog atas S3.","Salah — COPY memuat data ke Redshift, yang secara eksplisit dilarang oleh skenario.","Benar — External schema dari Data Catalog + Redshift Spectrum memungkinkan join data S3 dengan tabel lokal Redshift tanpa memuat data.","Salah — Membalik arah (unload Redshift ke S3 lalu query di Athena) menambah salinan data dan pipeline, padahal analis ingin bekerja di Redshift."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift + 'query S3 tanpa load' + Data Catalog → CREATE EXTERNAL SCHEMA FROM DATA CATALOG (Redshift Spectrum)."},{"id":"E3B-35","d":3,"ts":"3.3.6","t":"Step Functions retry and catch for pipelines","q":"An AWS Step Functions state machine starts an AWS Glue job that extracts data from an on-premises database. About once a week the job fails because of a transient network timeout, and an engineer must rerun it manually. The company wants the job to be retried automatically with increasing wait times, and the team must be notified only if all retries fail. Which TWO actions should a data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Add a Retry field to the Glue task state with an interval, a BackoffRate greater than 1, and a maximum number of attempts.","Add a Catch field to the Glue task state that transitions to a state that publishes a message to an Amazon SNS topic.","Create a CloudWatch alarm that notifies on every Glue job failure, including failures that are later retried successfully.","Increase the Glue job timeout to 48 hours.","Replace the state machine with a cron job on an Amazon EC2 instance."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Persyaratannya: 'retried automatically with increasing wait times' dan 'notified only if all retries fail'. Field Retry di Step Functions mendukung IntervalSeconds, BackoffRate (eksponensial bila lebih dari 1), dan MaxAttempts, sehingga kegagalan transien ditangani otomatis. Field Catch dievaluasi setelah semua retry habis, lalu mengalihkan alur ke state yang mempublikasikan pesan ke SNS. Distraktor terdekat adalah alarm CloudWatch untuk setiap kegagalan job — alarm itu juga akan berbunyi untuk percobaan yang akhirnya sukses setelah retry, melanggar 'only if all retries fail'. Menaikkan timeout tidak mengatasi timeout jaringan. Cron di EC2 menambah overhead. Aturan: error transien di Step Functions → Retry + BackoffRate; penanganan akhir → Catch.","r":["Benar — Retry dengan BackoffRate memberi percobaan ulang otomatis dengan jeda yang makin panjang.","Benar — Catch dijalankan setelah semua retry gagal dan mengarahkan ke notifikasi SNS.","Salah — Alarm per kegagalan akan memberi notifikasi meskipun retry berikutnya berhasil.","Salah — Timeout job tidak menyelesaikan gangguan jaringan transien.","Salah — Cron di EC2 menambah server yang harus dikelola dan kehilangan fitur retry bawaan."],"k":"Tips ujian: transient failure → Step Functions Retry (BackoffRate); notify after final failure → Catch → SNS."},{"id":"E4A-50","d":4,"ts":"4.2.4","t":"Lake Formation enforcement vs direct S3 access","q":"A data lake administrator uses AWS Lake Formation column-level permissions so that analysts cannot see the ssn column of a customer table when they query it with Amazon Athena. During an audit, the security team finds that analysts can still download the underlying Parquet files from the registered Amazon S3 location in the S3 console and read every column. What should the administrator do?","o":["Add a Lake Formation data filter that also excludes the ssn column.","Enable S3 Versioning on the bucket so that previous object versions cannot be read.","Move the ssn column into a separate Glue table that the analysts cannot query.","Remove direct Amazon S3 read permissions on the data lake location from the analysts' IAM policies so that data access happens only through Lake Formation-integrated services."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: analis bisa 'download the underlying Parquet files ... in the S3 console'. Lake Formation menegakkan izin kolom dan baris hanya untuk akses melalui service terintegrasi (Athena, Redshift Spectrum, EMR, Glue) yang meminta credential sementara dari Lake Formation. Jika IAM policy pengguna juga mengizinkan s3:GetObject langsung pada lokasi data, pengguna dapat melewati Lake Formation sepenuhnya. Solusinya adalah mencabut izin S3 langsung dari pengguna, sementara akses data diberikan lewat role yang mendaftarkan lokasi S3 di Lake Formation. Data filter tambahan tidak berpengaruh pada akses S3 langsung. Versioning tidak berkaitan dengan izin baca. Memindahkan kolom menambah pipeline dan tetap tidak mencegah akses file mentah lain. Aturan umum: Lake Formation hanya efektif jika pengguna tidak punya akses S3 langsung ke lokasi terdaftar.","r":["Salah — Data filter hanya berlaku untuk query lewat service terintegrasi, bukan unduhan S3 langsung.","Salah — Versioning tidak mengatur siapa yang boleh membaca objek.","Salah — Menambah pipeline dan tidak menutup celah akses S3 langsung.","Benar — Mencabut izin S3 langsung memaksa semua akses melewati Lake Formation sehingga izin kolom berlaku."],"k":"Tips ujian: pengguna melewati Lake Formation via S3 langsung → cabut s3:GetObject dari IAM pengguna."},{"id":"E3A-49","d":3,"ts":"3.2.2","t":"SageMaker Data Wrangler data cleaning","q":"A team of data scientists needs to clean and transform tabular training data from Amazon S3 and Amazon Redshift before building ML models. They want a visual interface with hundreds of built-in transformations, an automatic data quality and insights report (for example, target leakage and class imbalance warnings), and the ability to export the flow into an ML pipeline. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler (available in Amazon SageMaker Canvas).","Amazon Athena CTAS statements scheduled with EventBridge.","Amazon Quick Sight calculated fields.","AWS Lambda functions with pandas code triggered by S3 events."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'data scientists', 'visual interface with hundreds of built-in transformations', 'data quality and insights report' seperti target leakage dan class imbalance, serta 'export into an ML pipeline'. Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler (kini tersedia di dalam SageMaker Canvas) dirancang untuk persiapan data ML: bisa mengimpor data dari S3, Redshift, dan Athena, menyediakan ratusan transformasi visual, membuat Data Quality and Insights Report, dan mengekspor flow ke pipeline atau job pemrosesan. CTAS Athena memerlukan SQL dan tidak memberi insight khusus ML. Calculated fields Quick Sight untuk analitik BI, bukan persiapan data training. Lambda dengan pandas memerlukan kode dan tidak visual. Aturan umum: persiapan data visual untuk ML → SageMaker Data Wrangler; persiapan data visual untuk analitik umum → DataBrew.","r":["Benar — Data Wrangler menyediakan transformasi visual, laporan kualitas dan insight ML, serta ekspor ke pipeline.","Salah — Membutuhkan SQL dan tidak menyediakan laporan khusus ML seperti target leakage.","Salah — Calculated fields hanya untuk analisis BI dan tidak menghasilkan data training.","Salah — Membutuhkan kode kustom dan tidak menyediakan antarmuka visual atau laporan kualitas."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'data scientists + visual prep + target leakage/class imbalance report' → SageMaker Data Wrangler."},{"id":"E4B-39","d":4,"ts":"4.4.5","t":"Integrating CloudWatch Logs with Firehose and alarms","q":"A containerized data ingestion service on Amazon ECS sends its application logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The company needs (1) an alarm within minutes when the number of 'IngestionFailed' messages exceeds 50 in 5 minutes, and (2) a continuous copy of all log events delivered to Amazon S3 for long-term analysis with Amazon Athena. Which TWO actions meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Enable CloudTrail data events for Amazon ECS tasks.","Create an AWS Config rule that evaluates the log group every hour.","Create a metric filter on the log group for the pattern 'IngestionFailed' and a CloudWatch alarm on the resulting metric.","Run a script on an EC2 instance every 5 minutes that calls the CloudWatch Logs export API.","Create a subscription filter on the log group that sends the log events to Amazon Data Firehose for delivery to Amazon S3."],"a":[2,4],"e":"Ada dua kebutuhan terpisah: alarm 'within minutes' berdasarkan jumlah pesan tertentu, dan 'continuous copy' ke S3 untuk Athena, dengan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Metric filter mengubah kemunculan pola 'IngestionFailed' menjadi metric CloudWatch, dan alarm dengan threshold 50 per 5 menit memicu notifikasi. Subscription filter ke Amazon Data Firehose mengalirkan event log secara berkelanjutan ke S3 tanpa server untuk dikelola, sehingga Athena dapat meng-query-nya. Distraktor terdekat adalah skrip export di EC2: data sampai ke S3, tetapi Anda harus mengelola instance dan skrip, dan export task tidak dirancang untuk interval sangat sering. CloudTrail data events mencatat panggilan API, bukan isi log aplikasi. Config rule mengevaluasi konfigurasi resource, bukan isi log. Aturan umum: alert dari isi log → metric filter + alarm; streaming log ke S3 → subscription filter + Firehose.","r":["Salah — CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API, bukan pesan log aplikasi dari container.","Salah — Config mengevaluasi konfigurasi resource, bukan menghitung pesan di dalam log.","Benar — Metric filter + alarm memberi peringatan dalam hitungan menit berdasarkan jumlah pesan.","Salah — Skrip di EC2 menambah overhead operasional dibanding layanan terkelola.","Benar — Subscription filter + Firehose mengirim log terus-menerus ke S3 tanpa server untuk dikelola."],"k":"Tips ujian: log → alarm = metric filter; log → S3 continuous = subscription filter + Data Firehose."},{"id":"E3B-02","d":3,"ts":"3.3.5","t":"CloudTrail with CloudWatch Logs metric filters","q":"A company already has a CloudTrail trail that delivers management events to Amazon S3. The security team wants to be alerted within minutes whenever any API call in the data platform account fails with an AccessDenied error, and the alert must be sent by email. The team wants to avoid writing custom code. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Configure the trail to also deliver events to a CloudWatch Logs log group, create a metric filter on errorCode AccessDenied, and create a CloudWatch alarm that notifies an Amazon SNS email topic.","Schedule an Amazon Athena query every hour against the trail's S3 bucket and email the results by using an AWS Lambda function.","Enable Amazon Macie on the trail's S3 bucket and subscribe an email address to Macie findings.","Use the CloudTrail Event history console filter for error codes and check it daily."],"a":[0],"e":"Persyaratannya 'alerted within minutes', 'by email', dan 'avoid writing custom code'. Mengirim trail ke CloudWatch Logs memungkinkan metric filter (misalnya { $.errorCode = \"AccessDenied\" }) yang mengubah event menjadi metrik, lalu CloudWatch alarm mengirim notifikasi ke SNS topic dengan subscription email — semuanya konfigurasi, tanpa kode. Distraktor terdekat adalah query Athena terjadwal plus Lambda, tetapi itu per jam (bukan menit) dan butuh kode kustom. Macie mendeteksi data sensitif di S3, bukan error API. Pola klasik CIS benchmark: CloudTrail → CloudWatch Logs → metric filter → alarm → SNS.","r":["Benar — CloudTrail ke CloudWatch Logs + metric filter + alarm + SNS memberi notifikasi hampir real time tanpa kode kustom.","Salah — Query per jam terlalu lambat dan Lambda pengirim email menambah kode serta overhead operasional.","Salah — Macie mengklasifikasikan data sensitif di S3, bukan memantau error code panggilan API.","Salah — Pengecekan manual harian tidak memenuhi syarat alert dalam hitungan menit."],"k":"Tips ujian: alarm pada pola di log CloudTrail → kirim trail ke CloudWatch Logs + metric filter + alarm SNS."},{"id":"E1C-75","d":1,"ts":"1.4.10","t":"Data skew in distributed processing","q":"A Spark job on Amazon EMR joins a clickstream table with an orders table on customer_id. The Spark UI shows that 199 of 200 tasks in the join stage finish in about 1 minute, but one task runs for 2 hours and processes most of the data. A few customer IDs, including a default ID used for anonymous users, account for a large share of rows. Which combination of actions will reduce the job runtime? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Enable Spark adaptive query execution (AQE) with skew join optimization so that oversized partitions are split.","Increase the driver memory.","Add a random salt to the skewed join keys to spread the hot keys across multiple partitions, and expand the other side of the join accordingly.","Reduce the number of shuffle partitions to 10.","Use larger executors without changing the partitioning."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Gejalanya klasik 'data skew': hampir semua task cepat, tetapi 'one task runs for 2 hours' karena beberapa key (termasuk ID default anonim) mendominasi data. Dalam komputasi terdistribusi, satu stage selesai saat task terlambat selesai, sehingga satu partisi raksasa menentukan runtime. AQE dengan skew join optimization (Spark 3.x) mendeteksi partisi yang terlalu besar saat runtime dan memecahnya menjadi beberapa task. Salting menambahkan nilai acak ke key yang panas sehingga barisnya tersebar ke banyak partisi, dengan sisi lain join direplikasi untuk setiap nilai salt. Distractor terdekat adalah executor yang lebih besar: task raksasa mungkin sedikit lebih cepat, tetapi tetap dikerjakan oleh satu task. Mengurangi shuffle partitions justru memperbesar ukuran tiap partisi. Aturan umum: satu task lambat dalam stage → skew → AQE skew join atau salting (dan pertimbangkan memfilter key default).","r":["Benar — AQE memecah partisi yang terlalu besar saat runtime sehingga beban terbagi.","Salah — Join dijalankan di executor, bukan driver.","Benar — Salting menyebarkan hot key ke banyak partisi sehingga paralelisme pulih.","Salah — Partisi yang lebih sedikit membuat setiap partisi lebih besar dan skew tetap ada.","Salah — Partisi raksasa tetap diproses oleh satu task."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'one straggler task' → data skew → AQE skew join / salting."},{"id":"E2C-14","d":2,"ts":"2.4.2","t":"Iceberg schema evolution in Athena","q":"A data lake table stored as Parquet files and registered as a standard Hive-style table in the AWS Glue Data Catalog must have the column cust_nm renamed to customer_name. The table holds 80 TB of data and is queried with Amazon Athena. The company wants future column renames, additions, and drops to be metadata-only operations that do not rewrite data or break queries on historical files. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Rename the column in the Glue Data Catalog table definition and keep the existing Parquet files.","Migrate the table to Apache Iceberg format and then use ALTER TABLE ... CHANGE COLUMN in Athena for renames and other schema changes.","Create an Athena view that aliases cust_nm as customer_name and create a new view for every future change.","Rewrite the entire dataset with an AWS Glue job each time a column must be renamed."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah 'metadata-only operations' untuk rename, add, dan drop kolom tanpa merusak query pada file historis. Apache Iceberg melacak kolom berdasarkan ID unik, bukan berdasarkan nama atau posisi, sehingga rename, add, drop, dan reorder kolom hanya mengubah metadata dan file data lama tetap terbaca dengan benar. Athena mendukung DDL schema evolution untuk tabel Iceberg seperti ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMNS, DROP COLUMN, dan CHANGE COLUMN. Pada tabel Hive-style Parquet, Athena membaca kolom berdasarkan nama secara default, sehingga mengganti nama di Catalog membuat kolom tersebut bernilai NULL pada file lama. View alias bisa menjadi tambalan sementara tetapi menumpuk lapisan view dan tidak menyelesaikan kebutuhan jangka panjang. Menulis ulang 80 TB untuk setiap rename sangat mahal. Aturan umum: schema evolution yang aman dan metadata-only → open table format seperti Apache Iceberg.","r":["Salah — Parquet di tabel Hive-style dibaca berdasarkan nama kolom, sehingga file lama akan mengembalikan NULL untuk customer_name.","Benar — Iceberg memakai column ID sehingga rename/add/drop hanya mengubah metadata dan tetap konsisten dengan file lama.","Salah — Menumpuk view untuk setiap perubahan menambah kompleksitas dan tidak membuat schema evolution menjadi metadata-only.","Salah — Menulis ulang 80 TB setiap ada rename sangat mahal dan lambat."],"k":"Tips ujian: rename/drop kolom tanpa rewrite data → Apache Iceberg (column ID-based schema evolution)."},{"id":"E1A-20","d":1,"ts":"1.1.3","t":"Redshift COPY best practices","q":"A data engineer loads 200 GB of daily sales data from Amazon S3 into an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster that has 4 nodes with 16 slices in total. The data currently arrives as a single uncompressed 200 GB CSV file, and the COPY command takes too long. Which TWO actions will MOST improve load performance? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Load the data with many single-row INSERT statements in parallel.","Split the data into multiple files of roughly equal size, with the number of files a multiple of the number of slices.","Run a separate COPY command for each file at the same time on the same table.","Disable the cluster's automatic workload management.","Compress the files with GZIP or another supported compression format."],"a":[1,4],"e":"Kata kunci: 'single uncompressed 200 GB CSV file' dan cluster dengan '16 slices'. COPY memuat secara paralel per file di semua slice; dengan satu file besar, paralelisme hilang. Memecah data menjadi beberapa file berukuran hampir sama dengan jumlah kelipatan jumlah slice membuat semua slice bekerja seimbang. Kompresi (misalnya GZIP) mengurangi data yang dibaca dari S3 sehingga load lebih cepat. Distraktor terdekat adalah menjalankan beberapa COPY bersamaan ke tabel yang sama: Redshift men-serialisasi load tersebut, sehingga lebih lambat daripada satu COPY dengan prefix atau manifest. INSERT per baris sangat lambat untuk data warehouse kolumnar. Aturan umum: COPY cepat = satu perintah COPY, banyak file seimbang (kelipatan slice), terkompresi.","r":["Salah — INSERT satu baris sangat lambat dibandingkan COPY massal.","Benar — Banyak file seimbang (kelipatan slice) memungkinkan semua slice memuat secara paralel.","Salah — Beberapa COPY bersamaan ke tabel yang sama diserialisasi; gunakan satu COPY dengan prefix atau manifest.","Salah — WLM tidak memengaruhi paralelisme COPY untuk satu file besar.","Benar — Kompresi mengurangi volume data yang dibaca dari S3 dan mempercepat COPY."],"k":"Redshift COPY cepat → split file (kelipatan slice) + kompresi + satu COPY."},{"id":"E1A-24","d":1,"ts":"1.1.4","t":"Redshift Data API","q":"A data engineer is building an AWS Lambda function that runs short SQL queries against an Amazon Redshift Serverless workgroup and stores the results in Amazon S3. The function is invoked thousands of times per day. The engineer wants to avoid packaging JDBC drivers and managing database connections and connection pools. Which approach should the engineer use?","o":["Package the Redshift JDBC driver in a Lambda layer and open a new connection on each invocation.","Place an Amazon RDS Proxy in front of the Redshift workgroup.","Use the Amazon Redshift Data API to submit the SQL statements and retrieve results asynchronously.","Use Amazon Athena federated query to run the statements against Redshift."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'avoid packaging JDBC drivers' dan 'managing database connections'. Amazon Redshift Data API adalah API HTTPS yang memungkinkan menjalankan SQL secara asinkron tanpa koneksi persisten dan tanpa driver; autentikasi memakai IAM atau Secrets Manager, dan hasilnya diambil dengan panggilan API terpisah. Ini cocok untuk Lambda yang dipanggil sangat sering. Distraktor terdekat adalah JDBC di Lambda layer: berfungsi, tetapi melanggar persyaratan driver dan pengelolaan koneksi. RDS Proxy hanya mendukung engine RDS dan Aurora, bukan Redshift. Athena federated query menambah komponen dan tidak ditujukan untuk ini. Aturan umum: aplikasi serverless/event-driven ke Redshift tanpa koneksi = Redshift Data API.","r":["Salah — Melanggar persyaratan: perlu driver JDBC dan membuka koneksi di setiap invocation.","Salah — RDS Proxy tidak mendukung Amazon Redshift.","Benar — Redshift Data API berbasis HTTPS, asinkron, tanpa driver dan tanpa pengelolaan koneksi.","Salah — Athena federated query menambah lapisan yang tidak perlu dan tetap membutuhkan connector Lambda."],"k":"Lambda → Redshift tanpa JDBC/koneksi → Redshift Data API."},{"id":"E1C-27","d":1,"ts":"1.3.3","t":"Step Functions direct service integrations","q":"A Step Functions workflow currently invokes a small AWS Lambda function whose only purpose is to call DynamoDB PutItem to record the status of each pipeline run. The team wants to reduce the amount of code to maintain and lower cost. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Replace the Lambda task with a Step Functions task that uses the DynamoDB PutItem service integration directly.","Move the PutItem call into an AWS Glue Python shell job.","Increase the Lambda function memory so that it completes faster.","Replace the Lambda task with an Amazon SQS queue that a separate consumer reads to write to DynamoDB."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'only purpose is to call DynamoDB PutItem', 'reduce the amount of code', dan 'lower cost'. Step Functions mempunyai integrasi langsung (optimized integration dan AWS SDK integration) dengan lebih dari 200 layanan, termasuk DynamoDB PutItem, sehingga state machine bisa menulis item tanpa Lambda perantara. Ini menghapus kode, mengurangi biaya invocation Lambda, dan menghilangkan satu titik kegagalan. Distractor terdekat adalah menaikkan memori Lambda: fungsi masih ada sehingga kode dan biaya tetap ada. Glue Python shell job jauh lebih berat dan mahal untuk satu PutItem. Menambah SQS dan konsumen terpisah menambah komponen, bukan menguranginya. Aturan umum: jika Lambda hanya meneruskan panggilan API AWS, gunakan integrasi langsung Step Functions.","r":["Benar — Integrasi DynamoDB langsung menghapus Lambda perantara, mengurangi kode dan biaya.","Salah — Glue Python shell job adalah alat yang berlebihan untuk satu operasi tulis.","Salah — Lambda tetap harus dipelihara dan dibayar; memori tidak mengurangi kode.","Salah — Menambah antrean dan konsumen justru menambah komponen yang harus dikelola."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'Lambda hanya memanggil API AWS' → ganti dengan Step Functions service/SDK integration."},{"id":"E1B-59","d":1,"ts":"1.2.8","t":"Private APIs with API Gateway","q":"A data engineering team builds an internal data API with Amazon API Gateway and AWS Lambda that returns curated metrics from Amazon S3 and Amazon DynamoDB. Security policy requires that the API be reachable only from applications running inside the company's VPCs and never from the public internet. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create an edge-optimized REST API and restrict access with an API key.","Create a Regional REST API and publish its URL only on the internal wiki.","Create a private REST API in API Gateway, create an interface VPC endpoint for execute-api, and attach a resource policy that allows access only through that endpoint.","Create a Regional REST API with an AWS WAF rule that blocks requests from outside the corporate IP range."],"a":[2],"e":"Penentunya adalah API yang 'reachable only from applications running inside the company's VPCs and never from the public internet'. Private REST API di API Gateway hanya dapat diakses melalui interface VPC endpoint (AWS PrivateLink) untuk layanan execute-api, dan resource policy dapat membatasi akses hanya dari endpoint atau VPC tertentu. API edge-optimized atau Regional tetap memiliki endpoint publik; API key bukan mekanisme otorisasi dan tidak mencegah akses dari internet. Menyembunyikan URL bukan kontrol keamanan. WAF dapat memfilter IP, tetapi endpoint tetap publik sehingga melanggar persyaratan 'never from the public internet'. Aturan umum: API internal saja → API Gateway private API + interface VPC endpoint + resource policy.","r":["Salah — Endpoint edge-optimized bersifat publik, dan API key bukan kontrol akses jaringan.","Salah — Menyembunyikan URL bukan kontrol keamanan; endpoint tetap publik.","Benar — Private API hanya dapat diakses melalui interface VPC endpoint dan dibatasi dengan resource policy.","Salah — Endpoint tetap publik walaupun difilter dengan WAF."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'API only from inside VPC' → API Gateway private REST API + interface VPC endpoint (execute-api)."},{"id":"E1B-25","d":1,"ts":"1.2.3","t":"Athena Federated Query","q":"A data analyst must run a single ad hoc SQL query that joins clickstream data stored as Parquet in Amazon S3 with customer profiles in an Amazon DynamoDB table and order records in an Amazon RDS for MySQL database. The company does not want to build or schedule any ETL pipelines to copy the data first. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create AWS Glue ETL jobs that copy the DynamoDB and RDS data to Amazon S3, and then query all data with Amazon Athena.","Use AWS DMS to replicate the DynamoDB and RDS data into Amazon Redshift, and then load the S3 data with COPY.","Use Amazon Athena Federated Query with the DynamoDB and MySQL data source connectors, and join the sources in a single Athena query.","Export the DynamoDB table to S3 and take an RDS snapshot export to S3 every hour, and then query with Athena."],"a":[2],"e":"Penentunya adalah 'single ad hoc SQL query' atas tiga sumber berbeda dan larangan 'build or schedule any ETL pipelines to copy the data first'. Athena Federated Query memakai data source connector (berbasis Lambda) untuk DynamoDB, MySQL, dan sumber lain, sehingga satu query SQL dapat melakukan join antara data S3 dan sumber eksternal tanpa memindahkan data. Glue job yang menyalin ke S3 adalah distraktor terdekat karena hasil akhirnya tetap di-query dengan Athena, tetapi itu justru pipeline ETL yang dilarang. DMS ke Redshift dan export terjadwal juga membangun proses penyalinan dan menambah overhead. Aturan umum: query ad hoc lintas sumber tanpa ETL → Athena Federated Query.","r":["Salah — Membangun pipeline ETL penyalinan yang secara eksplisit tidak diinginkan.","Salah — DMS dan Redshift menambah replikasi dan infrastruktur untuk satu query ad hoc.","Benar — Athena Federated Query melakukan join lintas S3, DynamoDB, dan MySQL dalam satu query tanpa memindahkan data.","Salah — Export terjadwal adalah proses penyalinan berulang dan datanya bisa tertinggal hingga satu jam."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'query across S3 + DynamoDB/RDS/others with SQL, no data movement' → Athena Federated Query."},{"id":"E2C-13","d":2,"ts":"2.4.2","t":"Avro schema evolution rules (BACKWARD)","q":"A schema in the AWS Glue Schema Registry uses the Avro format with the BACKWARD compatibility mode. A data engineer must evolve the schema for the next producer release. Which TWO changes will the registry accept as a new schema version? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Add a new optional field that has a default value.","Rename an existing field without adding an alias.","Delete an existing field.","Add a new required field that has no default value.","Change the type of an existing field from string to int."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah mode BACKWARD, yang berarti consumer yang memakai schema baru harus tetap bisa membaca data yang ditulis dengan schema versi sebelumnya. Menghapus field aman karena reader dengan schema baru cukup mengabaikan field yang ada di data lama. Menambah field opsional dengan default value juga aman karena saat membaca data lama yang tidak memiliki field tersebut, reader memakai nilai default. Menambah field wajib tanpa default akan gagal karena data lama tidak memiliki nilai untuk field itu. Rename tanpa alias sama dengan menghapus satu field dan menambah field wajib baru, sehingga tidak kompatibel. Mengubah tipe dari string ke int bukan promosi tipe yang valid di Avro. Aturan umum: BACKWARD (default di Glue Schema Registry) → boleh delete field dan add optional field dengan default.","r":["Benar — Field opsional dengan default dapat diisi nilai default saat membaca data lama, jadi kompatibel BACKWARD.","Salah — Rename tanpa alias membuat reader baru mencari field yang tidak ada di data lama tanpa default.","Benar — Reader dengan schema baru cukup mengabaikan field yang dihapus saat membaca data lama.","Salah — Data lama tidak memiliki nilai untuk field wajib baru tanpa default, sehingga tidak bisa dibaca.","Salah — string ke int bukan promosi tipe yang didukung Avro dan memecah kompatibilitas."],"k":"Tips ujian: BACKWARD = consumer baru baca data lama → boleh hapus field / tambah field opsional dengan default."},{"id":"E2B-06","d":2,"ts":"2.2.2","t":"Cross-account Data Catalog sharing","q":"A central data lake account (Account A) catalogs curated tables in the AWS Glue Data Catalog, and AWS Lake Formation manages permissions. An analytics team in Account B must query two of those databases with Amazon Athena in Account B. The data must stay in Account A's S3 buckets, and Account A must keep control of permissions. Which TWO steps should the data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["In Account A, use Lake Formation to grant the two databases or their tables to Account B.","Enable S3 Cross-Region Replication from Account A's buckets to a bucket in Account B and run a crawler in Account B.","In Account B, create resource links in the local Glue Data Catalog that point to the shared databases, and query the resource links from Athena.","Create an AWS Glue JDBC connection in Account B that points to the Glue Data Catalog in Account A.","Export the Data Catalog of Account A to JSON files and import them into Account B with the CreateTable API."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'data must stay in Account A' dan 'Account A must keep control of permissions'. Pola standar berbagi technical catalog lintas akun adalah Lake Formation cross-account grant dari akun produsen ke akun konsumen. Di akun konsumen, admin membuat resource link di Glue Data Catalog lokal yang menunjuk ke database/tabel yang dibagikan, sehingga Athena di Account B bisa mereferensikannya seperti tabel lokal. Data tetap di S3 Account A dan izin tetap dikontrol dari Account A. Replikasi S3 lalu crawl ulang membuat salinan data dan catalog kedua, melanggar kedua syarat. Ekspor/impor definisi juga membuat catalog terpisah yang tidak sinkron. Glue JDBC connection dipakai untuk database, bukan untuk mengakses Data Catalog akun lain. Ingat: berbagi catalog lintas akun → Lake Formation grant + resource link.","r":["Benar — Lake Formation cross-account grant membagikan database/tabel sambil mempertahankan kontrol izin di Account A.","Salah — Replikasi menyalin data keluar dari Account A dan membuat catalog terpisah, melanggar syarat skenario.","Benar — Resource link di Account B memungkinkan Athena mereferensikan database yang dibagikan dari Account A.","Salah — JDBC connection untuk sumber data database, bukan cara mengakses Data Catalog akun lain.","Salah — Ekspor/impor definisi menghasilkan catalog salinan yang cepat tidak sinkron dan izinnya tidak dikontrol Account A."],"k":"Tips ujian: cross-account Data Catalog → Lake Formation grant ke akun konsumen + resource link di akun konsumen."},{"id":"E4B-14","d":4,"ts":"4.3.3","t":"Cross-account KMS with S3","q":"Account A owns an S3 bucket whose objects are encrypted with SSE-KMS using the AWS managed key aws/s3. An analytics role in Account B must read the objects. The bucket policy already grants s3:GetObject to the role, and the role's IAM policy allows the action, but every request fails with an AccessDenied error. What should the data engineer do to enable cross-account access?","o":["Create a customer managed KMS key in Account A whose key policy allows the Account B role to use kms:Decrypt, re-encrypt the objects with this key, and add kms:Decrypt on the key ARN to the role's IAM policy in Account B.","Edit the key policy of the aws/s3 key to allow the Account B role to use kms:Decrypt.","Change the objects to SSE-C and share the encryption key with Account B.","Enable S3 ACLs on the bucket and grant READ to the Account B canonical user ID."],"a":[0],"e":"Penyebab kegagalan terletak pada 'AWS managed key aws/s3': key policy AWS managed key tidak dapat diubah dan hanya mengizinkan principal dari akun yang sama, sehingga Account B tidak pernah bisa mendekripsi objek tersebut. Solusinya adalah memakai customer managed key yang key policy-nya memberi Account B izin kms:Decrypt, mengenkripsi ulang objek dengan kunci tersebut, lalu menambahkan izin kms:Decrypt pada IAM policy role di Account B. Akses KMS lintas akun selalu butuh dua sisi: key policy di akun pemilik dan IAM policy di akun pengguna. Distraktor terdekat adalah mengedit key policy aws/s3, yang tidak dimungkinkan. SSE-C memindahkan beban pengelolaan kunci ke pelanggan dan tidak praktis untuk layanan analitik. ACL hanya mengatur izin S3, bukan izin KMS, jadi error tetap terjadi. Aturan umum: SSE-KMS lintas akun → gunakan customer managed key, bukan AWS managed key.","r":["Benar — Customer managed key memungkinkan key policy lintas akun, ditambah IAM policy di Account B.","Salah — Key policy AWS managed key tidak dapat dimodifikasi.","Salah — SSE-C menuntut pengelolaan kunci manual di setiap request dan tidak cocok untuk analitik lintas akun.","Salah — ACL tidak memberikan izin KMS; dekripsi tetap ditolak."],"k":"Tips ujian: cross-account + objek dienkripsi aws/s3 → tidak bisa; ganti ke customer managed key."},{"id":"E2B-49","d":2,"ts":"2.3.4","t":"Suspending S3 Versioning","q":"A scratch S3 bucket used for temporary pipeline outputs has S3 Versioning enabled, and the noncurrent versions now make up 70% of the bucket's storage. The team no longer needs version history for this bucket and wants to stop accumulating versions and remove the existing ones automatically. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Disable versioning on the bucket so that S3 deletes all previous versions immediately.","Delete the bucket and create a new bucket with the same name.","Suspend versioning on the bucket and add a Lifecycle rule with NoncurrentVersionExpiration and removal of expired object delete markers.","Enable MFA Delete so that versions are no longer created."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'stop accumulating versions' dan 'remove the existing ones automatically'. Setelah diaktifkan, versioning S3 tidak bisa dimatikan kembali, hanya bisa di-suspend. Saat suspended, objek baru disimpan dengan version ID null sehingga tidak ada versi baru yang menumpuk, tetapi versi noncurrent yang sudah ada tetap tersimpan. Karena itu tambahkan Lifecycle rule NoncurrentVersionExpiration dan pembersihan expired delete markers untuk menghapus versi lama secara otomatis. Opsi 'disable' tidak tersedia. Menghapus dan membuat ulang bucket mengganggu pipeline dan berisiko kehilangan nama bucket. MFA Delete hanya menambah autentikasi untuk penghapusan versi. Ingat: versioning hanya bisa Enabled atau Suspended; data versi lama dibersihkan dengan lifecycle.","r":["Salah — Versioning tidak bisa dinonaktifkan setelah diaktifkan, dan suspend pun tidak menghapus versi lama.","Salah — Membuat ulang bucket mengganggu pipeline dan membutuhkan pengosongan bucket secara manual.","Benar — Suspend menghentikan versi baru, dan lifecycle menghapus versi noncurrent yang ada secara otomatis.","Salah — MFA Delete tidak menghentikan pembuatan versi dan justru mempersulit penghapusan."],"k":"Tips ujian: versioning tidak bisa 'disabled', hanya 'suspended'; versi lama tetap ada sampai dihapus lifecycle."},{"id":"E1C-50","d":1,"ts":"1.4.2","t":"Lambda provisioned concurrency","q":"A data enrichment API is implemented with Amazon API Gateway and an AWS Lambda function written in Java. During business hours (08:00–18:00), the API must meet a p99 latency target, but cold starts that take several seconds violate the target. Outside business hours, traffic is very low and cost must be minimized. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Configure provisioned concurrency on a function alias and use Application Auto Scaling scheduled actions to raise it before 08:00 and lower it after 18:00.","Configure reserved concurrency equal to the peak concurrency.","Increase the function timeout to 15 minutes.","Invoke the function every minute with an Amazon EventBridge schedule to keep exactly one environment warm."],"a":[0],"e":"Kebutuhannya: hilangkan 'cold starts' saat jam kerja untuk p99 latency, tetapi 'cost must be minimized' di luar jam kerja. Provisioned concurrency menyiapkan execution environment yang sudah terinisialisasi sehingga request tidak mengalami cold start; dengan Application Auto Scaling scheduled actions, jumlahnya dinaikkan sebelum 08:00 dan diturunkan setelah 18:00, sehingga Anda hanya membayar saat dibutuhkan. Distractor terdekat adalah ping EventBridge setiap menit: hanya menjaga satu environment hangat, sementara lonjakan concurrency tetap memicu cold start pada environment baru. Reserved concurrency membatasi dan mencadangkan kapasitas, tetapi tidak menginisialisasi environment sebelumnya. Timeout tidak terkait cold start. Aturan umum: cold start pada beban yang dapat diprediksi → provisioned concurrency dengan jadwal auto scaling.","r":["Benar — Provisioned concurrency menghilangkan cold start, dan jadwal auto scaling menekan biaya di luar jam kerja.","Salah — Reserved concurrency tidak menyiapkan environment yang hangat.","Salah — Timeout tidak berpengaruh pada waktu cold start.","Salah — Satu environment hangat tidak cukup untuk request paralel saat puncak."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'cold start' + 'predictable hours' → provisioned concurrency + scheduled Application Auto Scaling."},{"id":"E1A-36","d":1,"ts":"1.1.6","t":"S3 Event Notifications","q":"A company receives CSV files in the incoming/ prefix of an Amazon S3 bucket throughout the day. Each new .csv file must be processed within seconds of arrival by an AWS Lambda function. Other files, such as .tmp files in the same prefix, must be ignored. What is the SIMPLEST way to meet these requirements?","o":["Run an AWS Glue crawler every 5 minutes and invoke the Lambda function when new tables are found.","Schedule the Lambda function every minute to list the bucket and process new .csv files.","Configure an S3 Event Notification for s3:ObjectCreated:* events with prefix incoming/ and suffix .csv that invokes the Lambda function.","Enable S3 server access logging and parse the logs to find new files."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: diproses 'within seconds of arrival', hanya file '.csv' di 'incoming/', dan 'SIMPLEST'. S3 Event Notifications bisa memanggil Lambda langsung untuk event ObjectCreated dengan filter prefix dan suffix, sehingga file .tmp diabaikan tanpa kode tambahan. Distraktor terdekat adalah Lambda terjadwal yang me-list bucket: latensi hingga satu menit, biaya LIST, dan logika pelacakan file yang sudah diproses. Crawler mendeteksi skema, bukan file baru per objek. Server access logging dikirim dengan penundaan dan tidak cocok sebagai trigger. Aturan umum: memproses objek baru di S3 secara event-driven = S3 Event Notifications (filter prefix/suffix) → Lambda/SQS/SNS.","r":["Salah — Crawler mendeteksi skema, bukan objek baru, dan intervalnya terlalu lambat.","Salah — Polling terjadwal menambah latensi, biaya LIST, dan logika pelacakan.","Benar — Notifikasi S3 dengan filter prefix dan suffix memicu Lambda dalam hitungan detik untuk file .csv saja.","Salah — Access log dikirim dengan penundaan dan tidak dirancang sebagai trigger."],"k":"Objek baru di S3 → proses segera → S3 Event Notification (prefix/suffix filter) → Lambda."},{"id":"E4B-37","d":4,"ts":"4.4.4","t":"Logs Insights on historical JSON logs","q":"A data pipeline writes structured JSON log events, including a durationMs field, to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. A data engineer must calculate the 95th percentile of durationMs for each 1-hour interval over the past 7 days, using only the logs that already exist. The engineer wants to avoid building any new infrastructure. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create a metric filter that extracts durationMs and view the p95 statistic of the resulting metric for the past 7 days.","Create a subscription filter to stream the log group to Amazon OpenSearch Service and calculate the percentile there.","Run a CloudWatch Logs Insights query over the past 7 days that uses stats pct(durationMs, 95) by bin(1h).","Install the CloudWatch agent with a custom configuration to publish durationMs as a custom metric."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'using only the logs that already exist' untuk '7 days' dan 'avoid building any new infrastructure'. CloudWatch Logs Insights otomatis mengenali field dari log JSON, sehingga query seperti stats pct(durationMs, 95) by bin(1h) dapat langsung dijalankan pada data historis di log group. Distraktor terdekat adalah metric filter: memang dapat mengekstrak nilai numerik, tetapi metric filter hanya memproses log event yang masuk setelah filter dibuat (tidak retroaktif), sehingga data 7 hari terakhir tidak tercakup. Subscription filter ke OpenSearch juga hanya mengalirkan data baru dan butuh infrastruktur domain. CloudWatch agent untuk custom metric juga hanya berlaku ke depan dan menambah konfigurasi. Aturan umum: analisis historis atas log yang sudah ada di CloudWatch Logs → Logs Insights; metric/subscription filter tidak retroaktif.","r":["Salah — Metric filter tidak retroaktif; hanya log event baru yang menghasilkan metric.","Salah — Subscription filter hanya mengalirkan event baru dan membutuhkan domain OpenSearch tambahan.","Benar — Logs Insights meng-query field JSON historis dan mendukung fungsi pct() serta bin().","Salah — Custom metric dari agent hanya berlaku ke depan dan menambah konfigurasi baru."],"k":"Tips ujian: metric filter & subscription filter tidak retroaktif; analisis log historis → Logs Insights."},{"id":"E4B-27","d":4,"ts":"4.4.2","t":"CloudWatch agent and log retention","q":"A custom data ingestion application runs on a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances and writes application log files to local disk. The operations team needs the logs stored centrally, searchable within minutes of being written, and retained for 1 year. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Enable an AWS CloudTrail trail with data events for Amazon EC2.","Install the unified Amazon CloudWatch agent on the instances to send the log files to a CloudWatch Logs log group, and set the log group retention to 365 days.","Create a cron job on each instance that copies the log files to Amazon S3 every hour.","Create a daily Amazon EBS snapshot of the volumes that contain the log files."],"a":[1],"e":"Syarat penentu: log aplikasi harus 'stored centrally', 'searchable within minutes', dan 'retained for 1 year' dengan overhead terendah. CloudWatch agent membaca file log lokal dan mengirimnya hampir real-time ke CloudWatch Logs; log group mendukung retention setting (misalnya 365 hari) dan dapat dicari dengan filter atau CloudWatch Logs Insights. Distraktor terdekat adalah cron job ke S3: tersentral, tetapi delay hingga satu jam, harus dirawat di setiap instance, dan pencarian membutuhkan layanan tambahan. CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API AWS, bukan log aplikasi di dalam instance. Snapshot EBS bukan solusi logging dan tidak dapat dicari. Aturan umum: log aplikasi dari EC2/on-premises → CloudWatch agent → CloudWatch Logs dengan retention policy.","r":["Salah — CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API AWS, bukan isi log aplikasi di instance.","Benar — CloudWatch agent mengirim log hampir real-time ke log group yang dapat dicari dengan retention 365 hari.","Salah — Cron job menambah delay, perawatan per instance, dan tidak langsung bisa dicari.","Salah — Snapshot EBS tidak terpusat sebagai log dan tidak dapat dicari."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'application logs from EC2 centralized' → CloudWatch agent + CloudWatch Logs; CloudTrail ≠ application logs."},{"id":"E3A-14","d":3,"ts":"3.1.4","t":"AWS Glue Flex execution","q":"A company runs 30 AWS Glue Spark jobs every night for non-urgent reporting. The reports are needed by 08:00, and the jobs usually finish by 03:00. The jobs can tolerate delayed starts and longer runtimes. The company wants to reduce the cost of these jobs with the LEAST effort. What should a data engineer do?","o":["Rewrite the jobs to run on a long-running Amazon EMR cluster with On-Demand Instances.","Switch the jobs to the G.2X worker type to finish faster.","Configure the jobs to use the Flex execution class.","Disable auto scaling on the jobs and set a fixed number of workers."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'non-urgent', 'can tolerate delayed starts and longer runtimes', dan 'reduce cost with the LEAST effort'. Glue Flex execution class menjalankan job di kapasitas cadangan AWS dengan harga per DPU-hour yang lebih murah dibanding Standard, sebagai imbalan waktu mulai dan durasi yang tidak dijamin. Cukup ubah execution class tanpa mengubah kode. Memindahkan ke cluster EMR yang selalu menyala menambah biaya idle dan overhead pengelolaan. G.2X memberi kapasitas lebih besar per worker dengan tarif per worker yang lebih tinggi, jadi tidak otomatis lebih hemat. Mematikan auto scaling justru bisa membuat worker berlebih dibayar sia-sia. Aturan umum: Glue job yang tidak sensitif waktu (dev/test, batch malam) → Flex.","r":["Salah — Cluster EMR yang menyala terus menambah biaya idle dan pekerjaan migrasi.","Salah — Worker yang lebih besar menaikkan tarif per worker dan tidak ditujukan untuk menghemat biaya.","Benar — Flex memberi tarif lebih murah untuk job yang bisa menerima start tertunda, tanpa perubahan kode.","Salah — Tanpa auto scaling, worker tetap bisa berlebih dan malah menambah biaya."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue job 'non-urgent / flexible start time' + hemat biaya → Flex execution class."},{"id":"E2A-14","d":2,"ts":"2.1.2","t":"DynamoDB LSI","q":"A data engineer is designing a new Amazon DynamoDB table for support tickets with account_id as the partition key and created_at as the sort key. The application must also query tickets for one account sorted by priority, and these reads must be strongly consistent. Each account will store less than 1 GB of tickets. Which design meets these requirements?","o":["Create a global secondary index with account_id as the partition key and priority as the sort key after the table is created.","Create the table with a local secondary index that uses account_id as the partition key and priority as the sort key.","Use a Scan with ConsistentRead set to true and sort the results in the application.","Create a global secondary index with priority as the partition key and request strongly consistent reads on it."],"a":[1],"e":"Persyaratan yang menentukan adalah query 'for one account sorted by priority' (partition key sama, sort key berbeda) dan 'strongly consistent'. Local secondary index (LSI) memakai partition key yang sama dengan tabel dasar tetapi sort key alternatif, dan mendukung strongly consistent read. LSI harus didefinisikan saat tabel dibuat, dan karena tabel ini masih dirancang, hal itu tidak masalah; batas item collection 10 GB per partition key juga aman karena tiap akun di bawah 1 GB. Distraktor terdekat adalah GSI dengan account_id dan priority: struktur kuncinya cocok, tetapi GSI hanya mendukung eventually consistent read. Scan dengan ConsistentRead sangat boros. Aturan umum: sort key alternatif + strong consistency → LSI (dibuat saat create table, ingat batas 10 GB per item collection).","r":["Salah — GSI tidak mendukung strongly consistent read, sehingga syarat konsistensi gagal.","Benar — LSI berbagi partition key, menyediakan sort key alternatif, dan mendukung strongly consistent read; bisa dibuat karena tabel masih baru.","Salah — Scan membaca seluruh tabel dan menyortir di aplikasi tidak efisien serta mahal.","Salah — GSI tidak mendukung strongly consistent read, dan priority sebagai partition key berkardinalitas rendah dapat menyebabkan hot partition."],"k":"Same partition key + alternate sort key + strongly consistent → LSI (hanya saat pembuatan tabel)."},{"id":"E2A-59","d":2,"ts":"2.1.8","t":"pgvector IVFFlat vs HNSW parameters","q":"A data engineer uses pgvector in Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL. To limit memory use and index build time, the team must use an IVFFlat index. The engineer created the IVFFlat index on an empty table and then loaded 3 million embeddings. Similarity searches now return poor recall. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Increase the hnsw.ef_search setting for the session.","Drop and re-create the IVFFlat index after the data is loaded, choosing an appropriate number of lists, and tune ivfflat.probes at query time.","Keep the index and continue loading more rows so that the existing clusters rebalance automatically over time.","Increase the Aurora instance size so the index fits in memory."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci adalah index IVFFlat 'created ... on an empty table' lalu data dimuat, dan hasilnya 'poor recall'. IVFFlat menentukan centroid cluster (lists) saat index dibangun berdasarkan data yang ada; jika dibangun pada tabel kosong, centroid tidak merepresentasikan distribusi data sehingga vektor terkumpul di cluster yang buruk dan recall rendah. Panduan pgvector adalah membuat index IVFFlat setelah tabel berisi data, memilih jumlah lists yang sesuai, dan menaikkan ivfflat.probes saat query untuk menukar sedikit kecepatan dengan recall lebih tinggi. Distraktor terdekat adalah menaikkan hnsw.ef_search: parameter itu hanya berlaku untuk index HNSW, bukan IVFFlat. Centroid tidak diperbarui otomatis saat data bertambah, dan instance lebih besar tidak memperbaiki kualitas cluster. Aturan umum: IVF butuh data representatif untuk training/clustering; parameter query IVF = probes, HNSW = ef_search.","r":["Salah — hnsw.ef_search hanya memengaruhi index HNSW, bukan IVFFlat.","Benar — Membangun ulang IVFFlat setelah data dimuat menghasilkan centroid yang representatif, dan probes menyesuaikan recall saat query.","Salah — IVFFlat tidak menyeimbangkan ulang centroid secara otomatis saat data bertambah; vektor baru hanya dimasukkan ke cluster yang sudah ada.","Salah — Memori lebih besar tidak memperbaiki centroid yang buruk sehingga recall tetap rendah."],"k":"IVF/IVFFlat built on empty table → poor clusters; rebuild after data load, tune lists/probes."},{"id":"E3A-37","d":3,"ts":"3.2.1","t":"Quick Sight SPICE vs direct query","q":"A retail company stores curated sales data in Amazon Athena tables. About 400 business users need interactive dashboards that respond in under a second when they filter and drill down. The data is refreshed once every hour. The company wants to avoid scanning the data in Amazon S3 every time a user interacts with a dashboard. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Build the dashboards in Amazon Quick Sight with a direct query dataset on Athena.","Export the Athena query results to Microsoft Excel files in Amazon S3 every hour for users to download.","Build Amazon Managed Grafana dashboards that query Athena on every panel refresh.","Build the dashboards in Amazon Quick Sight (formerly Amazon QuickSight) with the dataset imported into SPICE, and schedule an hourly refresh."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'respond in under a second', '400 users', 'refreshed once every hour', dan 'avoid scanning S3 on every interaction'. SPICE adalah engine in-memory di Amazon Quick Sight; data diimpor sekali ke SPICE sehingga filter dan drill-down dilayani dari memori dengan cepat, tanpa query baru ke Athena. Refresh terjadwal setiap jam (atau incremental refresh) menjaga data tetap segar sesuai frekuensi pembaruan. Direct query mengirim query Athena pada setiap interaksi, sehingga lebih lambat dan menambah biaya pemindaian S3. Grafana yang query Athena setiap refresh panel punya masalah yang sama dan lebih cocok untuk metrik operasional. File Excel bukan dashboard interaktif. Aturan umum: dashboard BI yang cepat dan hemat atas data yang diperbarui berkala → Quick Sight + SPICE + refresh terjadwal.","r":["Salah — Direct query mengirim query Athena di setiap interaksi, lebih lambat dan memindai S3 berulang kali.","Salah — File Excel tidak interaktif dan tidak cocok untuk 400 pengguna dashboard.","Salah — Grafana akan query Athena terus-menerus dan dirancang untuk observabilitas, bukan BI bisnis.","Benar — SPICE melayani interaksi dari memori dan refresh per jam menjaga data tetap segar tanpa scan berulang."],"k":"Tips ujian: Quick Sight 'fast dashboards + avoid repeated source queries' → SPICE + scheduled/incremental refresh."},{"id":"E1C-63","d":1,"ts":"1.4.5","t":"CloudFormation StackSets","q":"A company uses AWS Organizations with 30 accounts. Every account must have the same baseline data lake resources: an encrypted Amazon S3 bucket, an AWS Glue database, and IAM roles. New accounts are created every month and must receive the same resources automatically. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Deploy the CloudFormation template manually in each account whenever an account is created.","Create an AWS CloudFormation StackSet with service-managed permissions that targets the organizational unit and has automatic deployment enabled.","Write a Python script that loops through all accounts and creates the resources with the AWS SDK.","Use AWS Config conformance packs to create the resources in each account."],"a":[1],"e":"Kebutuhannya: sumber daya yang sama di '30 accounts', akun baru harus 'receive the same resources automatically', dengan 'LEAST operational overhead'. CloudFormation StackSets men-deploy satu template ke banyak akun dan Region; dengan service-managed permissions yang terintegrasi dengan AWS Organizations dan automatic deployment, akun baru yang ditambahkan ke OU target otomatis mendapat stack. Distractor terdekat adalah script SDK: bisa membuat resource, tetapi tidak memiliki manajemen state, rollback, drift detection, maupun deployment otomatis ke akun baru. Deploy manual tidak skalabel dan rawan terlewat. Conformance pack AWS Config mengevaluasi kepatuhan konfigurasi, bukan membuat resource dasar. Aturan umum: IaC lintas banyak akun/Region → CloudFormation StackSets.","r":["Salah — Proses manual tidak otomatis dan rawan kesalahan.","Benar — StackSets dengan service-managed permissions dan automatic deployment menerapkan template ke semua akun, termasuk akun baru.","Salah — Script imperatif tidak memiliki manajemen state, rollback, atau deployment otomatis.","Salah — Conformance packs mengevaluasi kepatuhan, bukan menyediakan resource data lake."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'same resources across many accounts/Regions' + 'new accounts automatically' → CloudFormation StackSets."},{"id":"E1C-02","d":1,"ts":"1.3.1","t":"Amazon MWAA migration","q":"A company runs 200 Apache Airflow DAGs on a self-managed Airflow cluster on Amazon EC2. The operations team spends significant time patching the scheduler, scaling workers, and maintaining the metadata database. The company wants to move to a managed service while making minimal changes to the existing DAG code. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Rewrite each DAG as an AWS Step Functions state machine by using Amazon States Language.","Migrate the DAGs to Amazon Managed Workflows for Apache Airflow (Amazon MWAA) by uploading the DAG files, requirements.txt, and plugins to an Amazon S3 bucket.","Convert each DAG into an AWS Glue workflow with scheduled and conditional triggers.","Replace each DAG with an Amazon EventBridge Scheduler schedule that invokes AWS Lambda functions in sequence."],"a":[1],"e":"Syaratnya adalah 'managed service' dan 'minimal changes to the existing DAG code'. Amazon MWAA menjalankan Apache Airflow open source yang dikelola AWS: scheduler, worker, web server, dan metadata database dikelola, sedangkan DAG cukup diunggah ke folder S3 beserta requirements.txt dan plugins. Karena tetap Airflow, kode DAG Python bisa dipakai hampir tanpa perubahan. Distractor terdekat adalah Step Functions: memang managed, tetapi seluruh 200 DAG harus ditulis ulang ke Amazon States Language, sehingga melanggar syarat perubahan minimal. Glue workflows dan EventBridge Scheduler juga memerlukan desain ulang total dan tidak mendukung konsep DAG Airflow seperti sensor atau backfill. Aturan umum: jika sudah punya Airflow DAG dan ingin managed, jawabannya MWAA.","r":["Salah — Step Functions managed, tetapi menulis ulang 200 DAG ke ASL adalah perubahan kode besar.","Benar — MWAA menjalankan Airflow terkelola; DAG, requirements.txt, dan plugins dibaca dari S3 sehingga kode DAG nyaris tidak berubah.","Salah — Glue workflows hanya mengorkestrasi job/crawler Glue dan membutuhkan desain ulang semua DAG.","Salah — Rangkaian jadwal dan Lambda bukan pengganti DAG; dependensi, retry, dan backfill harus dibangun ulang secara manual."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'existing Airflow DAGs' + 'managed' → Amazon MWAA (DAG di S3)."},{"id":"E1A-13","d":1,"ts":"1.1.2","t":"AWS DataSync vs Snow Family","q":"A company has 400 TB of historical data in an on-premises Hadoop cluster (HDFS). The company has a 10 Gbps AWS Direct Connect link and must move the data to Amazon S3 within 3 weeks, followed by daily incremental copies of new and changed files until the cluster is decommissioned. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Order multiple AWS Snowball Edge devices for the initial copy and write custom scripts for the daily incremental copies.","Deploy an AWS DataSync agent on premises, create a task with an HDFS source location and an Amazon S3 destination, and schedule the task to run daily.","Run the Hadoop DistCp tool on the on-premises cluster every day to copy all files to Amazon S3.","Use AWS Transfer Family to create an SFTP server and upload the files from the Hadoop cluster."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: '10 Gbps Direct Connect', '400 TB dalam 3 minggu', dan 'daily incremental copies' dengan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Secara kasar, 10 Gbps mampu memindahkan sekitar 100 TB per hari, jadi 400 TB dalam 3 minggu realistis secara online. AWS DataSync mendukung HDFS sebagai lokasi sumber, menyalin hanya file yang baru atau berubah pada eksekusi berikutnya, memverifikasi integritas data, dan task-nya bisa dijadwalkan. Distraktor terdekat adalah Snowball Edge: berguna saat bandwidth terbatas, tetapi di sini jaringan cukup dan tetap butuh script kustom untuk incremental. DistCp manual berarti menulis dan memantau sendiri logika incremental dan retry. Transfer Family dirancang untuk mitra yang mengirim file via SFTP, bukan migrasi massal HDFS. Aturan umum: bandwidth memadai + transfer online terjadwal dan incremental = DataSync. Catatan pembaruan: AWS Snowball Edge kini tidak tersedia untuk pelanggan baru; AWS mengarahkan pelanggan baru ke DataSync untuk transfer online (atau AWS Data Transfer Terminal untuk transfer fisik).","r":["Salah — Snowball Edge tidak perlu bila bandwidth cukup, incremental harian tetap memerlukan script kustom, dan Snowball Edge kini tidak tersedia untuk pelanggan baru.","Benar — DataSync mendukung HDFS, transfer incremental, verifikasi, dan penjadwalan task secara managed.","Salah — DistCp bisa berfungsi, tetapi Anda harus mengelola sendiri penjadwalan, incremental, dan error handling.","Salah — Transfer Family ditujukan untuk transfer file via SFTP/FTPS, bukan migrasi HDFS skala besar."],"k":"On-prem NFS/SMB/HDFS → S3, bandwidth cukup, terjadwal/incremental → AWS DataSync."},{"id":"E1C-13","d":1,"ts":"1.3.2","t":"Step Functions Retry with backoff and jitter","q":"An AWS Step Functions workflow starts AWS Glue jobs. During busy periods the StartJobRun task fails with Glue.ConcurrentRunsExceededException because the job's maximum concurrency is reached. The failures are transient and usually clear within a few minutes. Many executions fail at the same moment and retry together. Which configuration will make the workflow MOST resilient to these errors?","o":["Add a Catch for Glue.ConcurrentRunsExceededException that moves directly to a Fail state.","Add a Retry for States.ALL with IntervalSeconds 1, MaxAttempts 100, and BackoffRate 1.","Set the Glue job's maximum concurrency to the highest value and remove all error handling.","Add a Retry for Glue.ConcurrentRunsExceededException with IntervalSeconds 30, BackoffRate 2.0, MaxAttempts 6, MaxDelaySeconds 300, and JitterStrategy FULL."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'transient', 'clear within a few minutes', dan 'retry together' (thundering herd). Retry yang ditargetkan pada error spesifik dengan exponential backoff (BackoffRate 2.0), batas MaxDelaySeconds, dan JitterStrategy FULL menyebarkan waktu retry secara acak sehingga eksekusi tidak menyerbu Glue pada saat yang sama. Distractor terdekat adalah Retry States.ALL dengan interval 1 detik tanpa backoff: retry terlalu agresif, memperparah kontensi, dan ikut mengulang error permanen yang seharusnya tidak diulang. Catch langsung ke Fail membuat kegagalan sementara menjadi kegagalan permanen. Menaikkan concurrency tanpa error handling tidak menjamin error tidak terjadi dan bisa melampaui kuota akun. Aturan umum: error transient → Retry spesifik + exponential backoff + jitter; error permanen → Catch.","r":["Salah — Kegagalan sementara langsung menjadi kegagalan eksekusi, padahal bisa pulih sendiri.","Salah — Tanpa backoff dan jitter, retry serentak memperburuk throttling, dan States.ALL ikut mengulang error yang tidak bisa pulih.","Salah — Batas concurrency tetap ada dan tanpa penanganan error eksekusi akan gagal saat batas tercapai.","Benar — Retry spesifik dengan exponential backoff, batas delay, dan jitter penuh mengatasi error sementara tanpa serbuan retry serentak."],"k":"Tips ujian: transient/throttling error di Step Functions → Retry + BackoffRate + JitterStrategy FULL."},{"id":"E2A-48","d":2,"ts":"2.1.6","t":"RDS row-level locking","q":"An online store uses Amazon RDS for MySQL with InnoDB. Two order-processing workers sometimes read the same product's stock level at the same time, both see 1 unit available, and both complete a sale, causing overselling. The company wants to fix this while keeping high concurrency for orders of different products. What should a data engineer recommend?","o":["Run LOCK TABLES products WRITE at the start of every order transaction.","Inside a transaction, read the product row with SELECT ... FOR UPDATE before decrementing the stock, and then commit.","Set the transaction isolation level to READ UNCOMMITTED.","Route the stock reads to a read replica to reduce contention on the primary."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci adalah race condition 'both see 1 unit available' dan keinginan 'keeping high concurrency for orders of different products'. SELECT ... FOR UPDATE di InnoDB mengambil row-level exclusive lock pada baris produk yang dibaca, sehingga worker kedua menunggu sampai transaksi pertama commit dan kemudian membaca stok yang sudah diperbarui; pesanan untuk produk lain tidak terhalang karena lock hanya pada baris tersebut. Distraktor terdekat adalah LOCK TABLES: mencegah oversell, tetapi mengunci seluruh tabel sehingga semua pesanan menjadi serial dan konkurensi turun drastis. READ UNCOMMITTED justru memperbolehkan dirty read dan memperburuk masalah. Read replica bersifat asinkron sehingga data stok bisa basi. Aturan umum: cegah lost update pada baris tertentu di RDS → pessimistic row lock (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE) atau optimistic locking dengan kolom versi; hindari table lock.","r":["Salah — Table lock mencegah oversell tetapi menyerialkan semua pesanan, sehingga konkurensi hilang.","Benar — Row-level lock melalui SELECT ... FOR UPDATE mencegah dua transaksi memperbarui stok yang sama sambil tetap mengizinkan produk lain diproses paralel.","Salah — READ UNCOMMITTED melemahkan isolasi dan memungkinkan dirty read; masalah oversell tidak teratasi.","Salah — Replica asinkron dapat mengembalikan stok yang basi dan tidak mengunci baris di primary."],"k":"Prevent concurrent updates to same row in RDS → SELECT ... FOR UPDATE (row lock), not LOCK TABLES."},{"id":"E1B-48","d":1,"ts":"1.2.7","t":"Splittable compression formats","q":"A partner delivers one 40 GB gzip-compressed CSV file to Amazon S3 every night. An AWS Glue Spark job with 30 workers processes the file, but the Spark UI shows that the read stage runs as a single task on one executor while the other executors are idle. Which solution will MOST improve processing time?","o":["Ask the partner to deliver the data as multiple smaller files or in a splittable format such as bzip2-compressed CSV or Parquet.","Increase the number of workers to 60.","Change the worker type to G.8X.","Enable AWS Glue Auto Scaling on the job."],"a":[0],"e":"Petunjuk kuncinya adalah 'one 40 GB gzip-compressed CSV file' dan 'runs as a single task'. Gzip bukan format kompresi yang splittable, sehingga Spark harus membaca seluruh file dengan satu task, dan semua executor lain menganggur. Solusinya adalah menerima data dalam banyak file yang lebih kecil atau memakai format splittable (misalnya bzip2, atau lebih baik Parquet dengan Snappy) agar pembacaan dapat diparalelkan. Menambah worker, memakai worker lebih besar, atau Auto Scaling adalah distraktor yang menggoda, tetapi tidak satu pun membuat file gzip dapat dibagi, jadi tahap baca tetap satu task. Aturan umum: satu file gzip besar = satu task; gunakan file terpisah atau format splittable/kolumnar.","r":["Benar — File terpisah atau format splittable memungkinkan banyak task membaca secara paralel.","Salah — Worker tambahan tetap menganggur karena file gzip hanya dibaca oleh satu task.","Salah — Worker lebih besar tidak membuat file gzip dapat dibagi.","Salah — Auto Scaling tidak membantu jika hanya ada satu task yang bisa berjalan."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'single large gzip file, one task' → gzip not splittable → split files atau gunakan bzip2/Parquet."},{"id":"E3A-02","d":3,"ts":"3.1.1","t":"Migrating Airflow to Amazon MWAA","q":"A company runs about 200 Apache Airflow DAGs on a self-managed Airflow cluster on Amazon EC2. The DAGs use several community provider packages. The operations team spends too much time patching and scaling the Airflow scheduler and workers. The company wants to move to a managed service while making the FEWEST changes to the existing DAG code. What should a data engineer do?","o":["Rewrite each DAG as an AWS Step Functions state machine and trigger them with Amazon EventBridge Scheduler.","Convert the DAGs into AWS Glue workflows with triggers and move the Python logic into Glue Python shell jobs.","Create an Amazon MWAA environment, upload the DAG files to the dags folder in the environment's S3 bucket, and list the provider packages in requirements.txt.","Package the Airflow scheduler and workers into containers and run them on Amazon ECS with AWS Fargate."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'FEWEST changes to the existing DAG code' dan 'managed service'. Amazon MWAA menjalankan Apache Airflow open-source secara terkelola, sehingga DAG yang ada bisa dipakai hampir tanpa perubahan. Anda cukup menaruh file DAG di folder dags pada bucket S3 environment, dan dependensi Python (misalnya provider packages) didaftarkan di requirements.txt. AWS mengelola scheduler, worker, web server, patching, dan autoscaling worker. Menulis ulang ke Step Functions atau Glue workflows berarti mengubah 200 DAG, bertentangan dengan syarat perubahan minimal. Menjalankan Airflow di ECS Fargate tetap self-managed: Anda masih mengurus metadata database, upgrade, dan scaling. Aturan umum: migrasi Airflow yang sudah ada → MWAA.","r":["Salah — Menulis ulang 200 DAG menjadi state machine adalah perubahan kode yang sangat besar.","Salah — Glue workflows bukan Airflow; semua logika DAG harus didesain ulang.","Benar — MWAA kompatibel dengan Airflow; DAG di-upload ke S3 dan dependensi lewat requirements.txt, infrastruktur dikelola AWS.","Salah — Container di Fargate mengurangi pengelolaan server tetapi Airflow-nya tetap Anda kelola sendiri (scheduler, database metadata, upgrade)."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'existing Airflow DAGs' + 'managed' → Amazon MWAA (DAG di S3, requirements.txt, plugins.zip)."},{"id":"E1B-16","d":1,"ts":"1.2.1","t":"ECS cost optimization","q":"A company runs nightly containerized data transformation tasks on an Amazon ECS cluster backed by an EC2 Auto Scaling group. The cluster sits idle for about 18 hours each day. The tasks are stateless and can be restarted if interrupted. Which TWO actions will reduce compute costs the MOST? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Run the tasks by using a Fargate Spot capacity provider.","Purchase 3-year Reserved Instances sized for the peak nightly capacity.","Increase the CPU and memory reservations of each task to the maximum supported values.","Move the container instances to EC2 Dedicated Hosts.","Use an ECS capacity provider with managed scaling so the Auto Scaling group scales in to zero instances when no tasks are running."],"a":[0,4],"e":"Faktor penentunya adalah cluster 'idle for about 18 hours each day' dan task yang 'can be restarted if interrupted'. Fargate Spot menjalankan task yang toleran interupsi dengan diskon besar dan tanpa membayar instance saat idle. Capacity provider dengan managed scaling membuat Auto Scaling group menyesuaikan jumlah instance dengan kebutuhan task, termasuk turun ke nol saat tidak ada task, sehingga biaya 18 jam idle hilang. Reserved Instance adalah distraktor terdekat karena memberi diskon, tetapi Anda tetap membayar kapasitas puncak sepanjang hari walaupun 75% waktu idle. Menaikkan reservasi CPU/memori ke maksimum justru membuang sumber daya, dan Dedicated Host lebih mahal. Aturan umum: beban batch interruptible dan idle panjang → Spot + scale to zero, bukan komitmen kapasitas tetap.","r":["Benar — Fargate Spot memberi diskon besar untuk task stateless yang dapat diulang, tanpa biaya instance idle.","Salah — RI tetap dibayar 24 jam walaupun cluster idle 18 jam per hari.","Salah — Over-provisioning task meningkatkan biaya tanpa manfaat.","Salah — Dedicated Host adalah opsi yang lebih mahal dan tidak mengurangi idle time.","Benar — Managed scaling menyesuaikan kapasitas dengan task dan bisa scale in ke nol saat tidak ada pekerjaan."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'idle most of the day + interruptible tasks' → Spot (Fargate Spot/EC2 Spot) + scale to zero."},{"id":"E3A-26","d":3,"ts":"3.1.7","t":"Athena query result reuse","q":"A dashboard runs the same set of Amazon Athena queries every time a user opens it. Hundreds of users open the dashboard during business hours, and the underlying data in Amazon S3 changes only once per hour. Athena costs are increasing. Which solution will reduce cost with the LEAST effort?","o":["Enable Athena query result reuse with a maximum age of up to 60 minutes for these queries.","Copy the data to Amazon Redshift and point the dashboard to Redshift.","Create an Amazon ElastiCache cluster and cache the query results from application code.","Run the queries less often by limiting the number of dashboard users."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'same queries', 'data changes only once per hour', dan 'LEAST effort'. Fitur query result reuse di Athena memungkinkan query identik memakai kembali hasil query sebelumnya yang masih berada dalam batas maximum age, tanpa memindai ulang data di S3. Karena Athena on-demand ditagih per data yang dipindai, melewati eksekusi berarti mengurangi biaya pemindaian. Reuse diaktifkan per query, hanya berlaku di workgroup yang sama, dengan maximum age default 60 menit (maksimum setara 7 hari). Mengatur maximum age sekitar 60 menit cocok dengan frekuensi perubahan data. Memindahkan data ke Redshift atau membangun cache di ElastiCache menambah infrastruktur dan kode. Membatasi pengguna mengorbankan kebutuhan bisnis. Aturan umum: query Athena yang berulang atas data yang jarang berubah → query result reuse.","r":["Benar — Result reuse mengembalikan hasil eksekusi sebelumnya di workgroup yang sama tanpa memindai ulang S3; cukup diaktifkan per query.","Salah — Migrasi ke Redshift menambah infrastruktur dan biaya yang tidak diperlukan.","Salah — ElastiCache membutuhkan cluster dan kode caching kustom.","Salah — Membatasi pengguna bertentangan dengan kebutuhan bisnis."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'identical Athena queries + data jarang berubah' → query result reuse."},{"id":"E3B-25","d":3,"ts":"3.3.7","t":"CloudWatch Logs data protection","q":"An AWS Glue job occasionally writes customer email addresses and credit card numbers into its CloudWatch Logs log group when it logs rejected records. Developers need to keep reading the logs for troubleshooting, but the sensitive values must be masked for anyone who is not explicitly authorized to unmask them. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST effort?","o":["Encrypt the log group with a customer managed AWS KMS key.","Enable Amazon Macie on the log group to redact the sensitive values.","Create a data protection policy on the log group that uses managed data identifiers for email addresses and credit card numbers.","Create a subscription filter that sends logs to a Lambda function that redacts the values and writes them to a new log group."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'masked for anyone who is not explicitly authorized to unmask' dan 'LEAST effort'. CloudWatch Logs data protection policy mendeteksi data sensitif dengan managed data identifiers (misalnya EmailAddress, CreditCardNumber) dan menyamarkan nilainya saat ditampilkan; hanya principal dengan izin logs:Unmask yang dapat melihat nilai aslinya. Distraktor terdekat adalah Lambda yang meredaksi lewat subscription filter: butuh kode, dan log asli yang belum diredaksi tetap tersimpan di log group sumber. Enkripsi KMS melindungi data at rest tetapi siapa pun yang punya izin baca tetap melihat nilai asli. Macie memindai bucket S3, bukan log group. Aturan: PII di CloudWatch Logs → data protection policy (masking).","r":["Salah — Enkripsi tidak menyamarkan nilai bagi pengguna yang punya izin membaca log.","Salah — Macie menemukan data sensitif di Amazon S3, tidak meredaksi log group CloudWatch Logs.","Benar — Data protection policy menyamarkan email dan nomor kartu kredit secara otomatis, dengan unmask hanya untuk principal berizin.","Salah — Butuh kode kustom dan log asli yang tidak teredaksi tetap ada di log group sumber."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'mask sensitive data in CloudWatch Logs' → log group data protection policy."},{"id":"E2A-36","d":2,"ts":"2.1.4","t":"Snow Family vs DataSync","q":"A media archive company must move 4 PB of historical files from its data center to Amazon S3 within 6 weeks. The site has only a 200 Mbps internet connection that is also used for daily operations, and Direct Connect is not available. Which solution should a data engineer recommend?","o":["Use AWS DataSync over the internet connection with bandwidth throttling.","Order multiple AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized devices, copy the data locally, and ship them to AWS.","Use Amazon S3 Transfer Acceleration with multipart uploads.","Set up an AWS Transfer Family SFTP server and upload the files in parallel."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci adalah volume '4 PB', tenggat '6 weeks', dan koneksi hanya '200 Mbps' yang juga dipakai untuk operasional. Pada 200 Mbps penuh, transfer 4 PB membutuhkan sekitar 5 tahun, sehingga semua metode online mustahil memenuhi tenggat. AWS Snowball Edge adalah perangkat transfer offline: data disalin secara lokal ke beberapa perangkat lalu dikirim ke AWS untuk diimpor ke S3, sehingga tidak bergantung pada bandwidth jaringan. Distraktor terdekat adalah DataSync: alat migrasi online terbaik ketika bandwidth memadai, tetapi di sini bandwidth menjadi batas mutlak. S3 Transfer Acceleration hanya mengoptimalkan rute jarak jauh, tidak menambah kapasitas link lokal. Aturan umum: hitung waktu transfer — jika bandwidth × waktu < volume data, gunakan Snow Family (offline). Catatan pembaruan: AWS Snowball Edge tidak lagi tersedia untuk pelanggan baru sejak 7 November 2025; pelanggan yang sudah ada tetap dapat memakainya, sedangkan pelanggan baru diarahkan ke AWS DataSync (online), AWS Data Transfer Terminal (transfer fisik), atau solusi AWS Partner. Snow Family tetap tercantum di exam guide DEA-C01, jadi jawaban ini tetap valid untuk ujian.","r":["Salah — Dengan 200 Mbps, transfer 4 PB memakan waktu bertahun-tahun meskipun memakai DataSync.","Benar — Snowball Edge memindahkan data skala petabyte secara offline sehingga tenggat 6 minggu dapat dipenuhi tanpa membebani jaringan.","Salah — Transfer Acceleration tidak menambah bandwidth link lokal 200 Mbps yang menjadi bottleneck.","Salah — Transfer Family tetap bergantung pada koneksi internet yang terlalu lambat untuk 4 PB."],"k":"Petabytes + low bandwidth + tight deadline → AWS Snowball Edge (offline transfer)."},{"id":"E2B-13","d":2,"ts":"2.2.1","t":"Glue push-down predicates with Data Catalog","q":"An AWS Glue ETL job runs every morning and must process only the previous day's data from a Data Catalog table that has 3 years of daily partitions (partition keys year, month, day) in Amazon S3. Currently the job reads the whole table and then filters the DataFrame, which takes 2 hours and increases DPU cost. Which change will reduce run time and cost MOST effectively?","o":["Increase the number of workers and switch the job to the G.2X worker type.","Read the table with create_dynamic_frame.from_catalog and pass a push_down_predicate on year, month, and day for the previous day.","Run an AWS Glue crawler before the job so that the Data Catalog has the latest statistics.","Read the S3 path directly with Spark instead of the Data Catalog table, and filter with a WHERE clause after loading."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'process only the previous day's data' dari tabel yang sudah dipartisi di Data Catalog, dan saat ini job 'reads the whole table and then filters'. Saat membaca dari catalog dengan create_dynamic_frame.from_catalog, Anda bisa memberi push_down_predicate pada kolom partisi; Glue lalu memakai metadata partisi di Data Catalog untuk hanya me-list dan membaca folder S3 yang cocok. Hasilnya data yang dibaca turun dari 3 tahun menjadi 1 hari, sehingga waktu dan DPU turun. Menambah worker hanya mempercepat pemindaian penuh dengan biaya lebih besar. Crawler tidak mengubah cara job membaca data. Membaca path S3 langsung lalu memfilter setelah load tetap memindai semua data. Ingat: Glue job + tabel berpartisi di catalog → push_down_predicate (partition pruning).","r":["Salah — Lebih banyak worker tetap memindai seluruh tabel; biaya per run justru naik.","Benar — Push-down predicate memakai partisi di Data Catalog untuk hanya membaca folder hari sebelumnya.","Salah — Crawler memperbarui metadata, tetapi tidak membuat job berhenti membaca seluruh data.","Salah — Memfilter setelah load tetap membaca seluruh data, dan job kehilangan manfaat metadata catalog."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue job baca sebagian partisi dari catalog → push_down_predicate (atau catalogPartitionPredicate)."},{"id":"E2C-37","d":2,"ts":"2.4.5","t":"Database indexing for query performance","q":"An Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL table used by an order service has 300 million rows. A new report runs a query that filters on customer_id and order_status, and the query plan shows a sequential scan that takes minutes. The table receives moderate write traffic. Which action will MOST improve the query's performance?","o":["Increase the Aurora instance size to the largest instance class.","Create a composite B-tree index on (customer_id, order_status).","Add an Aurora Replica and run the report on it without other changes.","Partition the table by order_status only."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah query plan yang menunjukkan 'sequential scan' untuk filter pada customer_id dan order_status. Index B-tree komposit pada kolom yang dipakai di WHERE memungkinkan PostgreSQL mencari baris secara langsung tanpa memindai seluruh 300 juta baris, dan urutan kolom dengan kolom yang lebih selektif (customer_id) di depan biasanya paling efektif. Dengan write traffic moderat, biaya pemeliharaan index tambahan dapat diterima. Instance yang lebih besar mempercepat sedikit tetapi tetap memindai seluruh tabel dan jauh lebih mahal. Aurora Replica memindahkan beban baca, tetapi query tetap melakukan sequential scan. Partisi berdasarkan order_status yang berkardinalitas rendah tidak membantu filter customer_id. Aturan umum: query lambat karena full scan pada kolom filter di database relasional → tambahkan index yang sesuai, dengan trade-off biaya tulis.","r":["Salah — Instance lebih besar mahal dan tetap memindai seluruh tabel.","Benar — Index komposit memungkinkan lookup langsung berdasarkan customer_id dan order_status tanpa full scan.","Salah — Replica hanya memindahkan beban; query tetap melakukan sequential scan.","Salah — Partisi pada kolom berkardinalitas rendah tidak membantu filter customer_id yang selektif."],"k":"Tips ujian: sequential scan pada kolom filter → buat index (komposit sesuai kolom WHERE)."},{"id":"E1A-59","d":1,"ts":"1.1.10","t":"SNS to SQS fan-out","q":"When a customer places an order, an order service must notify four independent systems: inventory, billing, shipping, and analytics. Each system processes messages at its own pace, must not lose messages if it is temporarily unavailable, and must be added or removed without changing the order service. Which design meets these requirements?","o":["The order service sends a message to each of the four Amazon SQS queues directly.","The order service invokes the four systems' AWS Lambda functions synchronously.","The order service writes to one Amazon SQS queue that all four systems poll.","The order service publishes to an Amazon SNS topic, and each system has its own Amazon SQS queue subscribed to the topic."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: satu event ke 'four independent systems', 'at its own pace', 'must not lose messages', dan 'added or removed without changing the order service'. Pola SNS + SQS fan-out: producer mempublikasikan sekali ke topic SNS, setiap sistem memiliki antrean SQS sendiri yang berlangganan topic, sehingga setiap sistem menerima salinan pesan, memprosesnya dengan kecepatan sendiri, dan pesan tetap tersimpan di antrean saat sistem sedang tidak tersedia. Menambah sistem baru cukup dengan subscription baru. Distraktor terdekat adalah producer mengirim ke empat antrean langsung: berfungsi, tetapi producer harus diubah setiap ada konsumen baru (tightly coupled). Satu antrean bersama membagi pesan antar-konsumen, bukan menyalin. Pemanggilan sinkron membuat order service bergantung pada ketersediaan semua sistem. Aturan umum: fan-out ke banyak konsumen yang tahan gangguan = SNS → banyak SQS.","r":["Salah — Producer harus diubah setiap kali konsumen ditambah atau dihapus (tight coupling).","Salah — Panggilan sinkron membuat producer gagal saat salah satu sistem tidak tersedia.","Salah — Satu antrean membagi pesan sehingga setiap sistem hanya menerima sebagian.","Benar — SNS + SQS fan-out menyalin pesan ke setiap konsumen secara tahan lama dan terlepas dari producer."],"k":"Satu event → banyak konsumen independen & tahan lama → SNS topic + SQS queue per konsumen."},{"id":"E3B-51","d":3,"ts":"3.4.2","t":"Glue Data Quality multi-dataset rules","q":"A company migrated a sales table from an on-premises database to Amazon S3 by using an AWS Glue job. Before decommissioning the source, the auditors require proof that the target has the same number of rows as a source snapshot and that the total of the amount column matches. Both datasets are available to a Glue job. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST custom code?","o":["Use AWS Glue Data Quality multi-dataset rules such as RowCountMatch and AggregateMatch that compare the primary dataset with the source snapshot as a reference dataset.","Write a PySpark script that counts and sums both datasets and compares the results with if statements.","Run a DataBrew profile job on the target only.","Compare the S3 object sizes of the target files with the database file sizes."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'same number of rows' dan 'total of the amount column matches' antara dua dataset, serta 'LEAST custom code'. AWS Glue Data Quality mendukung rule multi-dataset: RowCountMatch membandingkan jumlah baris dataset utama dengan dataset referensi, dan AggregateMatch membandingkan hasil agregasi seperti sum(amount) dengan sum(reference.amount). Hasilnya tercatat sebagai hasil evaluasi kualitas data yang bisa dijadikan bukti audit. Distraktor terdekat adalah script PySpark kustom — hasilnya sama tetapi butuh kode dan tidak memberi laporan DQ standar. Profiling hanya target tidak melakukan perbandingan. Ukuran file berbeda karena format dan kompresi. Aturan: rekonsiliasi sumber vs target → DQDL RowCountMatch / AggregateMatch / DatasetMatch.","r":["Benar — Rule multi-dataset membandingkan jumlah baris dan agregat dengan dataset referensi tanpa kode kustom.","Salah — Logika perbandingan kustom menambah kode yang harus ditulis dan dirawat.","Salah — Profiling satu dataset tidak membuktikan kesamaan dengan sumber.","Salah — Ukuran file dipengaruhi format dan kompresi sehingga tidak membuktikan kesamaan data."],"k":"Tips ujian: source vs target reconciliation di Glue DQ → RowCountMatch, AggregateMatch, DatasetMatch."},{"id":"E4A-31","d":4,"ts":"4.2.1","t":"Custom policy for S3 SSE-KMS reads","q":"An AWS Glue job reads Parquet files from the s3://finance-curated/ledger/ prefix. The bucket uses SSE-KMS with a customer managed key. The job role has the AWSGlueServiceRole managed policy, but the job fails with AccessDenied errors when it reads the files. Which TWO permissions should a data engineer add to a custom policy on the job role while following least privilege? (Choose TWO.)","o":["s3:GetObject on arn:aws:s3:::finance-curated/ledger/*.","s3:* on arn:aws:s3:::*.","kms:Decrypt on the ARN of the customer managed key that encrypts the bucket.","kms:* on all resources.","iam:PassRole on all resources."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'reads' file terenkripsi 'SSE-KMS with a customer managed key' dan 'least privilege'. Membaca objek SSE-KMS memerlukan dua hal: izin s3:GetObject pada objek, serta izin kms:Decrypt pada key yang mengenkripsi objek tersebut (key policy juga harus mengizinkan, yang umumnya mendelegasikan ke IAM). AWSGlueServiceRole sudah memberi s3:ListBucket pada semua resource, tetapi s3:GetObject hanya pada bucket/objek dengan pola nama aws-glue-* dan tidak memberi kms:Decrypt, sehingga custom policy diperlukan; s3:GetObject berlaku pada ARN objek (bucket/prefix/*). s3:* atau kms:* pada semua resource melanggar least privilege. iam:PassRole tidak berhubungan dengan pembacaan data. Aturan umum: data SSE-KMS = izin S3 + kms:Decrypt pada key ARN spesifik.","r":["Benar — GetObject pada ARN objek di prefix ledger/ memberi akses baca yang tepat; s3:ListBucket sudah disediakan AWSGlueServiceRole.","Salah — s3:* pada semua bucket jauh melebihi kebutuhan.","Benar — kms:Decrypt pada key spesifik dibutuhkan untuk mendekripsi objek SSE-KMS.","Salah — kms:* pada semua key melanggar least privilege.","Salah — PassRole tidak dibutuhkan untuk membaca data dan wildcard resource terlalu luas."],"k":"Tips ujian: AWSGlueServiceRole hanya memberi GetObject/PutObject pada bucket aws-glue-*; data di bucket lain dengan SSE-KMS → tambah s3:GetObject pada ARN objek + kms:Decrypt pada key ARN."},{"id":"E4A-38","d":4,"ts":"4.2.2","t":"Redshift Data API authentication","q":"An AWS Lambda function runs SQL statements on an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster by using the Amazon Redshift Data API. The security team does not want any database password to be stored or managed for this function, not even in a secrets store. Which solution meets this requirement?","o":["Store the database password in AWS Secrets Manager and pass the secret ARN to the Data API calls.","Store the database password in an AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store SecureString parameter and pass it in the SQL connection string.","Embed the password in the SQL statement by using CREATE USER ... PASSWORD and reuse it on each call.","Call the Data API with the cluster identifier and a database user name, and grant the function's execution role redshift:GetClusterCredentials for that database user."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'not want any database password to be stored or managed ... not even in a secrets store'. Redshift Data API mendukung dua metode autentikasi: secret ARN dari Secrets Manager, atau credential database sementara berbasis IAM. Pada metode kedua, Anda memberikan cluster identifier dan nama user database, lalu Data API memakai redshift:GetClusterCredentials dari role pemanggil untuk menghasilkan password sementara, sehingga tidak ada password yang disimpan (untuk Redshift Serverless dipakai GetCredentials pada workgroup). Opsi Secrets Manager adalah cara yang valid secara umum, tetapi tetap menyimpan password sehingga melanggar syarat. Parameter Store juga menyimpan password. Memasukkan password di SQL jelas tidak aman. Aturan umum: tanpa password sama sekali → temporary credentials via IAM (GetClusterCredentials).","r":["Salah — Metode ini valid untuk Data API, tetapi tetap menyimpan password di secrets store.","Salah — Tetap menyimpan password, dan Data API tidak memakai connection string.","Salah — Password dalam SQL terekspos di log dan riwayat query.","Benar — Credential sementara berbasis IAM menghilangkan kebutuhan menyimpan atau mengelola password."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift Data API → Secrets Manager ARN ATAU temporary credentials IAM (GetClusterCredentials); 'no stored password' = temporary credentials."},{"id":"E1C-16","d":1,"ts":"1.3.2","t":"SQS visibility timeout and DLQ","q":"An AWS Lambda function with a 5-minute timeout processes messages from an Amazon SQS standard queue that has a 30-second visibility timeout. Messages are frequently processed more than once, and some messages that always fail keep returning to the queue indefinitely. Which combination of changes will fix these issues? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Set the queue's visibility timeout to at least six times the function timeout.","Reduce the function timeout to 30 seconds so it matches the visibility timeout.","Convert the queue to an SQS FIFO queue without changing other settings.","Configure a redrive policy that moves messages to a dead-letter queue after a maxReceiveCount such as 5.","Enable long polling with a 20-second ReceiveMessageWaitTimeSeconds."],"a":[0,3],"e":"Ada dua gejala: pesan diproses 'more than once' dan pesan yang 'always fail keep returning'. Gejala pertama terjadi karena visibility timeout (30 detik) lebih pendek dari waktu proses Lambda (hingga 5 menit), sehingga pesan muncul lagi dan diambil invocation lain; AWS merekomendasikan visibility timeout minimal 6 kali timeout fungsi. Gejala kedua diatasi dengan redrive policy ke dead-letter queue setelah maxReceiveCount tertentu, sehingga poison message dipindahkan dan bisa dianalisis. Distractor terdekat adalah memperpendek timeout fungsi menjadi 30 detik: pekerjaan yang butuh waktu lama akan gagal karena timeout. FIFO tanpa perubahan lain tetap mengalami masalah visibility yang sama. Long polling hanya mengurangi respons kosong dan biaya, tidak mengatasi duplikasi. Aturan umum: SQS + Lambda → visibility timeout ≥ 6× timeout fungsi, dan selalu sediakan DLQ.","r":["Benar — Visibility timeout yang cukup panjang mencegah pesan terlihat lagi selama masih diproses.","Salah — Pekerjaan yang butuh beberapa menit akan selalu timeout dan gagal.","Salah — FIFO tidak memperbaiki visibility timeout yang terlalu pendek dan bisa mengurangi throughput.","Benar — DLQ dengan maxReceiveCount mengeluarkan poison message dari antrean utama untuk dianalisis.","Salah — Long polling mengurangi panggilan kosong, bukan duplikasi atau poison message."],"k":"Tips ujian: SQS + Lambda duplikat → visibility timeout ≥ 6× function timeout; pesan gagal terus → DLQ."},{"id":"E4A-02","d":4,"ts":"4.1.1","t":"Security group referencing for Lambda to Redshift","q":"An AWS Lambda function that runs in private subnets of a VPC must run SQL statements against an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster in the same VPC on port 5439. The security team requires the narrowest possible network access so that only this function can reach the cluster. Which security group configuration meets these requirements?","o":["Add an inbound rule to the Redshift security group that allows TCP 5439 from the entire VPC CIDR block.","Add an outbound rule to the Redshift security group that allows TCP 5439 to the Lambda function's security group.","Add an inbound rule to the network ACL of the Redshift subnet that allows TCP 5439 from the Lambda subnets.","Add an inbound rule to the Redshift security group that allows TCP 5439 with the Lambda function's security group as the source."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'narrowest possible network access' dan 'only this function'. Security group bisa memakai security group lain sebagai source, sehingga hanya ENI yang memakai security group Lambda yang diizinkan masuk ke port 5439, berapa pun IP-nya. Ini lebih ketat dan lebih tahan perubahan daripada CIDR, karena IP ENI Lambda bisa berubah-ubah. Mengizinkan seluruh CIDR VPC berfungsi, tetapi semua resource di VPC ikut bisa menjangkau cluster sehingga melanggar syarat least privilege. Outbound rule di sisi Redshift tidak relevan karena koneksi diinisiasi oleh Lambda, dan security group bersifat stateful sehingga traffic balasan otomatis diizinkan. Aturan umum: untuk akses antar-resource di AWS, referensikan security group sumber, bukan rentang IP.","r":["Salah — Rule ini berfungsi tetapi terlalu luas karena semua resource di VPC bisa mengakses cluster.","Salah — Koneksi datang dari Lambda ke Redshift, jadi yang dibutuhkan inbound rule di Redshift; outbound di Redshift tidak membuka akses masuk.","Salah — Network ACL bekerja di level subnet dan tidak bisa membedakan satu fungsi tertentu; inbound security group Redshift juga tetap harus mengizinkan traffic.","Benar — Source berupa security group Lambda membatasi akses tepat ke fungsi tersebut dan tetap valid walau IP ENI berubah."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'only resource X can connect' → inbound rule dengan source = security group X, bukan CIDR."},{"id":"E2A-25","d":2,"ts":"2.1.3","t":"MemoryDB for fast key/value access","q":"A real-time bidding platform needs a primary database for user profile and feature data that is accessed by key. Reads must complete in microseconds, the application already uses Redis data structures and commands, and no data may be lost if a node fails. The company does not want to maintain a separate durable database behind a cache. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Amazon ElastiCache for Redis OSS in front of Amazon RDS for MySQL","Amazon DynamoDB with on-demand capacity","Amazon MemoryDB","Amazon Aurora MySQL with the query cache enabled"],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'primary database', 'microseconds' untuk read, 'Redis data structures and commands', 'no data may be lost', dan tidak ingin 'separate durable database behind a cache'. Amazon MemoryDB adalah database in-memory yang kompatibel dengan Redis OSS/Valkey dengan durabilitas Multi-AZ melalui transaction log terdistribusi, sehingga bisa dipakai sebagai database utama dengan read latensi mikrodetik dan write milidetik satu digit. Distraktor terdekat adalah ElastiCache di depan RDS: latensi mikrodetik dan kompatibel Redis, tetapi itu adalah arsitektur cache + database terpisah yang justru ingin dihindari, dan cache tidak dirancang sebagai penyimpanan primer yang durable. DynamoDB memberi latensi milidetik, bukan mikrodetik, dan tidak memakai API Redis. Aurora bukan key-value in-memory. Aturan umum: Redis-compatible + durable primary DB + mikrodetik → MemoryDB; cache saja → ElastiCache.","r":["Salah — Ini arsitektur cache plus database terpisah yang ingin dihindari, dan cache bukan penyimpanan utama yang durable.","Salah — DynamoDB memberikan latensi milidetik satu digit, bukan mikrodetik, dan tidak kompatibel dengan perintah Redis.","Benar — MemoryDB kompatibel Redis, membaca dalam mikrodetik, dan durable Multi-AZ sehingga cocok sebagai database utama.","Salah — Aurora adalah database relasional berbasis disk; tidak memberikan akses key-value mikrodetik dengan struktur data Redis."],"k":"Durable in-memory primary DB, Redis-compatible, microsecond reads → Amazon MemoryDB."}]});